    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30205\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"14\" y=\"20\" width=\"100\" height=\"70\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A \u22a5 B: \u2119(A\u2229B) = \u2119(A) \u2119(B)</text><rect x=\"26\" y=\"36\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"36\" width=\"40\" height=\"38\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B</text><rect x=\"126\" y=\"20\" width=\"100\" height=\"70\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A \u22a5 B | C: inside C only</text><rect x=\"136\" y=\"30\" width=\"80\" height=\"52\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e5e9f0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">C</text><ellipse cx=\"160\" cy=\"58\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(0 160 58)\"/><ellipse cx=\"188\" cy=\"58\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(0 188 58)\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A: I'm late   B: my friend is late</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dependent in general, independent given C: same jam</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Left: A and B with \u2119(A\u2229B) = \u2119(A)\u2119(B). Right: inside the case C (a jam), A and B satisfy \u2119(A\u2229B|C) = \u2119(A|C)\u2119(B|C), though they may be dependent overall.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Marginal Independence:</strong> $A \\perp B \\iff \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B) = \\mathbb{P}(A)\\,\\mathbb{P}(B)$, which is equivalent to $\\mathbb{P}(A \\mid B) = \\mathbb{P}(A)$ when $\\mathbb{P}(B) > 0$.",
      "<strong>Conditional Independence:</strong> $A \\perp B \\mid C \\iff \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B \\mid C) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\mid C)\\,\\mathbb{P}(B \\mid C)$.",
      "<strong>Zero Implication:</strong> Events independent marginally can become dependent given evidence (collider conditioning); events dependent marginally can become independent given their common cause."
    ],
    "math": "$$A \\perp B \\iff \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B) = \\mathbb{P}(A)\\mathbb{P}(B); \\qquad A \\perp B \\mid C \\iff \\mathbb{P}(A \\cap B \\mid C) = \\mathbb{P}(A \\mid C)\\mathbb{P}(B \\mid C)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two people late on the same bus.</strong> Whether you and a friend on the same route are late are linked, because of the jam. Once you know there was a jam, your lateness says nothing more about theirs.",
    "examTrap": "Berkson's Paradox: conditioning on common success (e.g. college admissions) creates artificial negative correlation between two independent skills.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Independence and conditional independence.</b> Events $A,B$ are independent if $\\mathbb P(A\\cap B)=\\mathbb P(A)\\mathbb P(B)$ (equivalently $\\mathbb P(A\\mid B)=\\mathbb P(A)$ when $\\mathbb P(B)\\gt 0$). Given an event $C$ with $\\mathbb P(C)\\gt 0$, $A$ and $B$ are conditionally independent given $C$ if $\\mathbb P(A\\cap B\\mid C)=\\mathbb P(A\\mid C)\\mathbb P(B\\mid C)$. Neither implies the other (Ross 3.4; Grimmett 1.5).",
    "hint": "When does learning that B happened tell you nothing about A, and how can a third fact change that?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(A\\cap B)=\\mathbb P(A)\\mathbb P(B)$ = knowing B leaves A unchanged.</strong> The joint chance is just the product of the two separate chances.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(A\\cap B\\mid C)$ = the same test inside the case $C$.</strong> It asks whether $A$ and $B$ still tell you nothing about each other once you know $C$.",
      "<strong>Neither way implies the other.</strong> Two events can be dependent overall and independent given $C$ (a shared cause), or independent overall and dependent given $C$."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
