    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30301\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30301)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30301)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x min</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">F(x)</text><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"226.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><path d=\"M24.0,111.3 L28.0,111.1 L32.1,110.9 L36.1,110.6 L40.2,110.3 L44.2,109.9 L48.2,109.4 L52.3,108.7 L56.3,107.9 L60.4,107.0 L64.4,105.8 L68.4,104.4 L72.5,102.7 L76.5,100.7 L80.6,98.3 L84.6,95.5 L88.6,92.4 L92.7,88.8 L96.7,84.8 L100.8,80.5 L104.8,76.0 L108.8,71.4 L112.9,66.6 L116.9,62.0 L121.0,57.6 L125.0,53.4 L129.0,49.6 L133.1,46.2 L137.1,43.2 L141.2,40.6 L145.2,38.4 L149.2,36.5 L153.3,35.0 L157.3,33.7 L161.4,32.6 L165.4,31.7 L169.4,31.0 L173.5,30.4 L177.5,29.9 L181.6,29.5 L185.6,29.2 L189.6,29.0 L193.7,28.8 L197.7,28.6 L201.8,28.5 L205.8,28.4 L209.8,28.3 L213.9,28.3 L217.9,28.2 L222.0,28.2 L226.0,28.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"76.9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"76.9\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"76.9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"76.9\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"72.93589734283444\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">F(x) = \u2119(X \u2264 x)</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">never decreases</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21921 as x\u2192\u221e, \u21920 as x\u2192\u2212\u221e</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X = ride time; F(x) = chance the ride is at most x minutes</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The CDF F(x) climbs from 0 to 1 as x (ride minutes) grows. The marked point shows F(x) = \u2119(X \u2264 x) read off at one x.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Measurable Mapping:</strong> A random variable $X: \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is a measurable function satisfying $\\{\\omega : X(\\omega) \\le x\\} \\in \\mathcal{F}$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$.",
      "<strong>CDF Definition:</strong> $F_X(x) \\triangleq \\mathbb{P}(X \\le x) = \\mathbb{P}(\\{\\omega \\in \\Omega : X(\\omega) \\le x\\})$.",
      "<strong>Four Invariants:</strong> (1) Non-decreasing: $x_1 \\le x_2 \\implies F(x_1) \\le F(x_2)$; (2) Right-continuous: $\\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} F(x+h) = F(x)$; (3) $\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} F(x) = 0$; (4) $\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} F(x) = 1$."
    ],
    "math": "$$F_X(x) = \\mathbb{P}(X \\le x), \\quad \\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} F_X(x+h) = F_X(x), \\quad F_X(-\\infty) = 0, \\quad F_X(\\infty) = 1$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Ride time as a number per morning.</strong> Each morning gets its ride time in minutes. The CDF then answers \u201cwhat share of mornings take at most 30 minutes?\u201d for every length at once, a curve that only goes up.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming CDFs must be continuous everywhere. Jump discontinuities F(x) - F(x\u207b) = P(X = x) occur at every discrete atom; only RIGHT-continuity is universally guaranteed!",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Random variable and CDF.</b> A random variable on $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ is a function $X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ such that $\\{X\\le x\\}\\in\\mathcal F$ for all $x$. Its cumulative distribution function is $F_X(x)=\\mathbb P(X\\le x)$. Then $F_X$ is non-decreasing and right-continuous, with $F_X(-\\infty)=0$ and $F_X(\\infty)=1$, and $F_X(x)-F_X(x^-)=\\mathbb P(X=x)$ (Ross 4.1; Grimmett 2.1).",
    "hint": "How do you turn the minutes your ride takes into one curve that answers \u201cat most this long\u201d for every x?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ = a number read off each morning.</strong> The ride time of that morning: each point of $\\Omega$ is sent to its length in minutes.",
      "<strong>$F_X(x)=\\mathbb P(X\\le x)$ = chance the ride takes at most $x$ minutes.</strong> It collects all mornings with ride time up to $x$.",
      "<strong>$F_X(-\\infty)=0,\\ F_X(\\infty)=1$ = it climbs from nothing to everything.</strong> It never decreases, and it is right-continuous: a jump is exactly the chance of one exact value."
    ],
