    "title": "Worked Benchmark: Mixed Random Variable & Lebesgue Splitting",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30306\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30306)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30306)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">wait x (min)</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">F(x)</text><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"226.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"112\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"60\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M24.0,60.0 L28.0,57.3 L32.1,54.8 L36.1,52.5 L40.2,50.4 L44.2,48.5 L48.2,46.8 L52.3,45.2 L56.3,43.7 L60.4,42.4 L64.4,41.2 L68.4,40.0 L72.5,39.0 L76.5,38.1 L80.6,37.2 L84.6,36.4 L88.6,35.7 L92.7,35.1 L96.7,34.5 L100.8,33.9 L104.8,33.4 L108.8,32.9 L112.9,32.5 L116.9,32.1 L121.0,31.8 L125.0,31.5 L129.0,31.2 L133.1,30.9 L137.1,30.7 L141.2,30.4 L145.2,30.2 L149.2,30.0 L153.3,29.9 L157.3,29.7 L161.4,29.6 L165.4,29.4 L169.4,29.3 L173.5,29.2 L177.5,29.1 L181.6,29.0 L185.6,28.9 L189.6,28.8 L193.7,28.8 L197.7,28.7 L201.8,28.6 L205.8,28.6 L209.8,28.5 L213.9,28.5 L217.9,28.4 L222.0,28.4 L226.0,28.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">jump \u03b1 = bus already there (wait 0)</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(1\u2212\u03b1)Fcont: bus still to come</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F = \u03b1\u00b7F(step) + (1\u2212\u03b1)\u00b7F(smooth): point mass plus density</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The CDF of the wait: a jump of size \u03b1 at 0 (the bus is already there), then a smooth rise F_cont weighted by 1 \u2212 \u03b1 up to 1.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem Setup:</strong> Waiting time $X$ has point mass $\\mathbb{P}(X=0) = 0.3$, point mass $\\mathbb{P}(X=1) = 0.3$, and uniform density $f_c(x) = 0.4$ for $x \\in (0, 1)$.",
      "<strong>CDF Structure:</strong> $F_X(x)$ jumps from 0 to 0.3 at $x=0$, rises linearly with slope 0.4 to 0.7 at $x=1^-$, then jumps by 0.3 to 1.0 at $x=1$.",
      "<strong>Expectation Evaluation:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\sum_k x_k \\mathbb{P}(X=x_k) + \\int_0^1 x f_c(x)\\,dx = 0(0.3) + 1(0.3) + \\int_0^1 0.4 x\\,dx = 0.3 + 0.2 = 0.5$."
    ],
    "math": "$$F_X(x) = \\alpha F_{\\text{disc}}(x) + (1-\\alpha) F_{\\text{cont}}(x), \\quad \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\sum_k x_k \\mathbb{P}(X=x_k) + \\int x f_c(x)\\,dx$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Sometimes the bus is just there.</strong> Some mornings you walk up and the bus is open at the stop: wait 0. On the others you wait some random time. The waiting time is part \u201cexactly 0\u201d and part \u201cany positive amount\u201d.",
    "examTrap": "Applying \u222b x f(x)dx alone without accounting for point mass jumps! Disregarding atoms F(x) - F(x\u207b) completely invalidates expected values and variances.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Mixed random variable.</b> A random variable whose CDF has the form $F_X=\\alpha F_{\\rm disc}+(1-\\alpha)F_{\\rm cont}$, $0\\lt \\alpha\\lt 1$, with $F_{\\rm disc}$ a step function and $F_{\\rm cont}$ continuous, is mixed. Its mean is $\\mathbb E[X]=\\sum_kx_k\\,\\mathbb P(X=x_k)+\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty x\\,f_c(x)\\,dx$, the atoms plus the continuous part, where $f_c$ is the density of the continuous part (Ross 5.1; Grimmett 4.1).",
    "hint": "With some chance the bus is already waiting, otherwise you wait a continuous time. How does that shape the CDF?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\alpha F_{\\rm disc}$ = the bus is already there.</strong> With chance $\\alpha$ the wait is exactly 0, so the CDF jumps at 0 by $\\alpha$.",
      "<strong>$(1-\\alpha)F_{\\rm cont}$ = otherwise you wait a continuous time.</strong> With chance $1-\\alpha$ the wait has a density and the CDF rises smoothly.",
      "<strong>$\\sum x_k\\mathbb P(X=x_k)+\\int xf_c$ = the mean has two parts.</strong> The atom contributes value times mass and the continuous part contributes the integral; dropping the atom gives a wrong mean."
    ],
