    "cardNumber": "02",
    "category": "JACOBIAN FORMULA",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Monotonic Transformation & The 1D Jacobian",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30402\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30402)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30402)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x (ride min)</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y = g(x) speed</text><path d=\"M40.0,102.0 L43.6,97.4 L47.2,93.2 L50.8,89.2 L54.4,85.4 L58.0,81.9 L61.6,78.6 L65.2,75.5 L68.8,72.7 L72.4,69.9 L76.0,67.4 L79.6,65.0 L83.2,62.8 L86.8,60.7 L90.4,58.8 L94.0,57.0 L97.6,55.3 L101.2,53.7 L104.8,52.2 L108.4,50.8 L112.0,49.4 L115.6,48.2 L119.2,47.1 L122.8,46.0 L126.4,45.0 L130.0,44.0 L133.6,43.1 L137.2,42.3 L140.8,41.5 L144.4,40.8 L148.0,40.1 L151.6,39.5 L155.2,38.9 L158.8,38.3 L162.4,37.8 L166.0,37.3 L169.6,36.8 L173.2,36.4 L176.8,36.0 L180.4,35.6 L184.0,35.3 L187.6,34.9 L191.2,34.6 L194.8,34.3 L198.4,34.0 L202.0,33.8 L205.6,33.5 L209.2,33.3 L212.8,33.1 L216.4,32.9 L220.0,32.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"90.0\" y1=\"118.0\" x2=\"90.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"118.0\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"50.2\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"90.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"50.2\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"50.2\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dx</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"57.586454964628146\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">dy</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">fY(y) = fX(x) |dx/dy|</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x = g\u207b\u00b9(y)</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">|\u00b7| keeps it positive</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">same area over dx and dy</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A decreasing map y = g(x) from ride time x to speed y. A band dx at x maps to a band dy, and the same chance sits over both: f_Y(y) = f_X(x) |dx/dy| with x = g\u207b\u00b9(y).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>1-to-1 Mapping:</strong> If $g$ is strictly monotonic and continuously differentiable on the support of $X$, the inverse $x = g^{-1}(y)$ exists uniquely.",
      "<strong>Mass Conservation:</strong> Probability in an infinitesimal interval must match: $f_Y(y)|dy| = f_X(x)|dx| \\implies f_Y(y) = f_X(g^{-1}(y)) \\left|\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|$.",
      "<strong>Reciprocal Derivative Form:</strong> Expressing via derivative of $g$: $f_Y(y) = \\frac{f_X(g^{-1}(y))}{|g'(g^{-1}(y))|}$ for all $y$ in the image of $g$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_Y(y) = f_X\\left(g^{-1}(y)\\right) \\left| \\frac{d}{dy} g^{-1}(y) \\right| = \\frac{f_X(g^{-1}(y))}{|g'(g^{-1}(y))|}, \\quad y \\in g(\\text{supp}(X))$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Minutes into speed.</strong> The chance in a band of ride times is the same chance in the matching band of speeds; the density changes by the stretch factor.",
    "examTrap": "Omitting the absolute value |dx/dy| for strictly decreasing functions (e.g. Y = -X or Y = 1/X). Probabilities and densities must NEVER be negative!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Monotone change of variables.</b> If $g$ is strictly monotone and differentiable on the support of $X$, then $Y=g(X)$ has density $f_Y(y)=f_X(g^{-1}(y))\\left|\\frac{d}{dy}g^{-1}(y)\\right|$ for $y\\in g(\\operatorname{supp}X)$ (Ross 5.7; Grimmett 4.7).",
    "hint": "If speed is distance over ride time, how does the density of the ride time turn into the density of the speed?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_X(g^{-1}(y))$ = density at the ride time that gives $y$.</strong> Undo $g$ to find which ride time $x$ produces speed $y$.",
      "<strong>$|\\frac{d}{dy}g^{-1}(y)|$ = how the axis stretches.</strong> A band $dy$ of speeds comes from a band $dx$ of ride times.",
      "<strong>$|\\cdot|$ = widths are positive.</strong> For decreasing $g$, $dx/dy$ is negative; the absolute value keeps the density non-negative."
    ],
