    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30501\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"84\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30501)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30501)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x min</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x)</text><path d=\"M24.0,81.6 L27.4,80.8 L30.7,79.8 L34.1,78.6 L37.5,77.2 L40.8,75.4 L44.2,73.4 L47.6,71.0 L50.9,68.3 L54.3,65.2 L57.7,61.8 L61.0,58.2 L64.4,54.3 L67.8,50.3 L71.1,46.2 L74.5,42.2 L77.9,38.3 L81.2,34.7 L84.6,31.4 L88.0,28.6 L91.3,26.5 L94.7,24.9 L98.1,24.1 L101.4,24.1 L104.8,24.8 L108.2,26.2 L111.5,28.3 L114.9,31.0 L118.3,34.2 L121.6,37.7 L125.0,41.6 L128.4,45.6 L131.7,49.7 L135.1,53.7 L138.5,57.6 L141.8,61.3 L145.2,64.7 L148.6,67.8 L151.9,70.6 L155.3,73.0 L158.7,75.1 L162.0,76.9 L165.4,78.4 L168.8,79.7 L172.1,80.7 L175.5,81.5 L178.9,82.1 L182.2,82.6 L185.6,83.0 L189.0,83.3 L192.3,83.5 L195.7,83.6 L199.1,83.7 L202.4,83.8 L205.8,83.9 L209.2,83.9 L212.5,83.9 L215.9,84.0 L219.3,84.0 L222.6,84.0 L226.0,84.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"76\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[g(X)] = \u222b g(x) f(x) dx</text><rect x=\"24\" y=\"104\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">walk \ud835\udd3c[A]</text><rect x=\"78\" y=\"104\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e5e9f0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"111\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">wait \ud835\udd3c[W]</text><rect x=\"144\" y=\"104\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"182\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">ride \ud835\udd3c[R]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[\u2211c\u1d62X\u1d62] = \u2211c\u1d62\ud835\udd3c[X\u1d62]: means add, always</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The density f(x) of one leg, with its mean \ud835\udd3c[X] marked. Below, the average walk, wait and ride lie end to end: \ud835\udd3c[\u2211c\u1d62X\u1d62] = \u2211c\u1d62\ud835\udd3c[X\u1d62].",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Center of Mass:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[X] \\triangleq \\int_\\Omega X(\\omega) d\\mathbb{P}(\\omega) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty x\\,dF_X(x)$. Exists if and only if $\\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$.",
      "<strong>LOTUS:</strong> To compute the expected value of $g(X)$, you do NOT need the density of $g(X)$: $\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty g(x) f_X(x)\\,dx$ (Law of the Unconscious Statistician).",
      "<strong>Universal Linearity:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[\\sum_{i=1}^n c_i X_i] = \\sum_{i=1}^n c_i \\mathbb{E}[X_i]$ holds for ANY random variables, requiring ZERO independence assumptions."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty g(x) f_X(x)\\,dx, \\qquad \\mathbb{E}\\left[\\sum_{i=1}^n c_i X_i\\right] = \\sum_{i=1}^n c_i \\mathbb{E}[X_i]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The average trip is the sum of the average parts.</strong> Average walk, average wait, average ride: add them and you have the average door-to-door time, with no need to know how the three are tangled together.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming E[g(X)] = g(E[X]). By Jensen's inequality, this holds only for linear/affine functions; for non-linear convex g, E[g(X)] \u2265 g(E[X]).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>LOTUS and linearity of expectation.</b> If $X$ has density $f_X$ (or pmf $p_X$) and $\\mathbb E|g(X)|\\lt \\infty$, then $\\mathbb E[g(X)]=\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty g(x)f_X(x)\\,dx$ (respectively $\\sum_xg(x)p_X(x)$). For random variables $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ with finite means and constants $c_i$, $\\mathbb E\\bigl[\\sum_ic_iX_i\\bigr]=\\sum_ic_i\\mathbb E[X_i]$, with no independence needed (Ross 4.4, 7.2; Grimmett 3.3).",
    "hint": "Can you add the average of the walk, the wait and the ride to get the average trip, and do you need to know the law of the sum?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\int g(x)f_X(x)\\,dx$ = weight each value by its density.</strong> To average a function of the ride time, you do not need the law of $g(X)$: use the density of $X$ itself.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_ic_i\\mathbb E[X_i]$ = means add up.</strong> The mean of walk plus wait plus ride is the sum of the three means, whatever the pieces are.",
      "<strong>No independence needed.</strong> Linearity holds even if a long wait and a long ride tend to come together; only variances care about that link."
    ],
