    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30505\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30505)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30505)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G(s)</text><path d=\"M24.0,95.2 L27.6,94.1 L31.2,93.0 L34.8,91.9 L38.4,90.7 L42.0,89.6 L45.6,88.3 L49.2,87.1 L52.8,85.8 L56.4,84.5 L60.0,83.1 L63.6,81.7 L67.2,80.3 L70.8,78.9 L74.4,77.4 L78.0,75.9 L81.6,74.4 L85.2,72.8 L88.8,71.2 L92.4,69.6 L96.0,67.9 L99.6,66.2 L103.2,64.5 L106.8,62.7 L110.4,60.9 L114.0,59.1 L117.6,57.3 L121.2,55.4 L124.8,53.5 L128.4,51.5 L132.0,49.5 L135.6,47.5 L139.2,45.5 L142.8,43.4 L146.4,41.3 L150.0,39.2 L153.6,37.0 L157.2,34.8 L160.8,32.6 L164.4,30.3 L168.0,28.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"95.2\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"107.2\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G(0) = \u2119(X = 0)</text><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"28.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">slope at s = 1:</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G\u2032(1) = \ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G(s) = \ud835\udd3c[s^X] = \u2211 \u2119(X = k) s\u1d4f</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N stops, X boarders each: G(s) = G\u2099(G\u2093(s))</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The PGF G(s) = \u2211\u2119(X = k)s\u1d4f rises from \u2119(X = 0) at s = 0 to 1 at s = 1. Its slope G\u2032(1) at the right end is \ud835\udd3c[X].",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Definition:</strong> For $X \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, $G_X(s) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[s^X] = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty p_k s^k$. Always converges absolutely for all $|s| \\le 1$ with $G_X(1) = 1$.",
      "<strong>Probability Extraction:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(X = k) = \\frac{1}{k!} G_X^{(k)}(0)$. Moments: $\\mathbb{E}[X] = G_X'(1)$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X) = G_X''(1) + G_X'(1) - (G_X'(1))^2$.",
      "<strong>Random Sums (Branching):</strong> If $S_N = \\sum_{i=1}^N X_i$ with $X_i$ i.i.d. and independent of $N$, then $G_{S_N}(s) = G_N(G_X(s))$ (functional composition)."
    ],
    "math": "$$G_X(s) = \\mathbb{E}[s^X] = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X=k) s^k, \\quad \\mathbb{E}[X] = G_X'(1), \\quad G_{\\sum_{i=1}^N X_i}(s) = G_N(G_X(s))$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Counting boarders.</strong> The number of passengers boarding at a stop is a whole number. A polynomial whose coefficients are the chances of 0, 1, 2, ... boarders holds the whole picture; its slope at 1 is the average crowd.",
    "examTrap": "Evaluating moments at s = 0 instead of s = 1! G_X(0) = P(X = 0), while expectations and variances require derivatives evaluated at s = 1.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Probability generating function.</b> For $X$ taking values in $\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$, $G_X(s)=\\mathbb E[s^X]=\\sum_{k\\ge0}\\mathbb P(X=k)s^k$ for $|s|\\le1$. Then $G_X(0)=\\mathbb P(X=0)$, $G_X(1)=1$, $\\mathbb E[X]=G_X'(1)$, and for independent $X_i$ with $N$ independent of them, $G_{\\sum_{i=1}^NX_i}(s)=G_N\\bigl(G_X(s)\\bigr)$ (Ross 7.7; Grimmett 5.1).",
    "hint": "How can a polynomial in s hold the whole count distribution, and how do you read the average off it?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum\\mathbb P(X=k)s^k$ = the count's law as a polynomial.</strong> The coefficient of $s^k$ is the chance of exactly $k$ boarders.",
      "<strong>$G_X(0)=\\mathbb P(X=0)$ and $G_X(1)=1$ = the endpoints.</strong> At $s=0$ only the empty count survives; at $s=1$ the chances add to 1.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[X]=G_X'(1)$ = the mean is the slope at 1.</strong> Differentiate at $s=1$, not at 0; plugging $G_X$ into $G_N$ handles a random number of terms."
    ],
