    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30702\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30702)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30702)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"17\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><polygon points=\"42,84 96,84 104,50 56,46\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">region A of (wait, ride) pairs</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30702)\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30702)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x, y)</text><path d=\"M130.0,97.6 L132.4,96.5 L134.8,95.0 L137.2,93.0 L139.6,90.5 L142.0,87.5 L144.4,83.8 L146.8,79.6 L149.2,74.7 L151.6,69.5 L154.0,64.0 L156.4,58.6 L158.8,53.3 L161.2,48.6 L163.6,44.7 L166.0,41.9 L168.4,40.3 L170.8,40.1 L173.2,41.2 L175.6,43.6 L178.0,47.2 L180.4,51.7 L182.8,56.8 L185.2,62.2 L187.6,67.7 L190.0,73.0 L192.4,78.0 L194.8,82.5 L197.2,86.3 L199.6,89.6 L202.0,92.3 L204.4,94.4 L206.8,96.0 L209.2,97.2 L211.6,98.1 L214.0,98.8 L216.4,99.2 L218.8,99.5 L221.2,99.7 L223.6,99.8 L226.0,99.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><polygon points=\"150.0,73.0 152.0,68.6 154.0,64.0 156.0,59.5 158.0,55.0 160.0,50.9 162.0,47.2 164.0,44.2 166.0,41.9 168.0,40.5 170.0,40.0 172.0,40.5 174.0,41.9 176.0,44.2 178.0,47.2 180.0,50.9 182.0,55.0 184.0,59.5 186.0,64.0 188.0,68.6 190.0,73.0 190.0,108.0 150.0,108.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">volume over A</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119((X,Y) \u2208 A) = \u222c f dx dy</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Left: a region A of (wait, ride) pairs. Right: a slice of the density f(x,y) over A. The volume under f above A is \u2119((X,Y) \u2208 A) = \u222cf dx dy.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Mixed Derivative:</strong> If $F_{X,Y}$ is differentiable, the joint PDF is $f_{X,Y}(x, y) = \\frac{\\partial^2 F_{X,Y}(x, y)}{\\partial x \\partial y}$.",
      "<strong>Volume Representation:</strong> For any Borel region $A \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2$, $\\mathbb{P}((X, Y) \\in A) = \\iint_A f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dx\\,dy$.",
      "<strong>Normalization:</strong> $f_{X,Y}(x, y) \\ge 0$ everywhere and total volume $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dx\\,dy = 1$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{X,Y}(x, y) = \\frac{\\partial^2 F_{X,Y}(x, y)}{\\partial x \\partial y}, \\qquad \\mathbb{P}((X, Y) \\in A) = \\iint_A f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dx\\,dy$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A hill over the plane.</strong> Over the wait-and-ride plane stands a hill whose height says how common each pair is. The chance of a set of pairs, such as \u201cshort wait but long ride\u201d, is the volume of hill above that set.",
    "examTrap": "Swapping integration order in non-rectangular domains without adjusting boundaries! For coupled domains like 0 \u2264 x \u2264 y \u2264 1, \u222b\u2080\u00b9 dx \u222b_x\u00b9 dy = \u222b\u2080\u00b9 dy \u222b\u2080^y dx.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Joint density.</b> $X,Y$ are jointly continuous if there is $f_{X,Y}\\ge0$ with $\\mathbb P((X,Y)\\in A)=\\iint_Af_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy$ for all (Borel) sets $A\\subset\\mathbb R^2$; then $f_{X,Y}(x,y)=\\dfrac{\\partial^2F_{X,Y}(x,y)}{\\partial x\\,\\partial y}$ where it exists, and $\\iint f_{X,Y}=1$ (Ross 6.1; Grimmett 4.5).",
    "hint": "How do you turn a region of (wait, ride) pairs into a chance when both can be any real value?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ = chance per unit area of the plane.</strong> A high spot means that combination of wait and ride is common.",
      "<strong>$\\iint_Af_{X,Y}\\,dx\\,dy$ = the volume above $A$.</strong> The chance of landing in a region is the volume under the surface over that region.",
      "<strong>$\\partial^2F/\\partial x\\,\\partial y$ = recover the density.</strong> Differentiate the joint CDF once in each variable; the total volume is 1."
    ],
