    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30704\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30704)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30704)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"11\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"62\" rx=\"36\" ry=\"26\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-25 70 62)\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x fixed</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30704)\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"26\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30704)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(y | x)</text><path d=\"M150.0,107.0 L151.9,106.6 L153.8,106.0 L155.7,105.1 L157.6,104.1 L159.5,102.7 L161.4,101.0 L163.3,98.9 L165.2,96.4 L167.1,93.4 L169.0,90.1 L170.9,86.3 L172.8,82.2 L174.7,77.9 L176.6,73.5 L178.5,69.2 L180.4,65.1 L182.3,61.4 L184.2,58.4 L186.1,56.0 L188.0,54.5 L189.9,54.0 L191.8,54.4 L193.7,55.8 L195.6,58.1 L197.5,61.1 L199.4,64.7 L201.3,68.8 L203.2,73.1 L205.1,77.5 L207.0,81.8 L208.9,85.9 L210.8,89.7 L212.7,93.1 L214.6,96.1 L216.5,98.7 L218.4,100.8 L220.3,102.6 L222.2,104.0 L224.1,105.0 L226.0,105.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><polygon points=\"160.0,102.3 163.0,99.3 166.0,95.2 169.0,90.1 172.0,84.0 175.0,77.2 178.0,70.3 181.0,63.9 184.0,58.6 187.0,55.2 190.0,54.0 193.0,55.2 196.0,58.6 199.0,63.9 202.0,70.3 205.0,77.2 208.0,84.0 211.0,90.1 214.0,95.2 217.0,99.3 220.0,102.3 220.0,108.0 160.0,108.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"8\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">area = 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(y | x) = f(x, y) / fX(x): slice, then divide by the slice's area</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Slicing the joint blob at a fixed wait x gives the curve f(y|x) on the right, with area 1: f(y|x) = f(x,y)/fX(x), the slice divided by its own area.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> For any $x$ with $f_X(x) > 0$, the conditional PDF of $Y$ given $X=x$ is $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x) \\triangleq \\frac{f_{X,Y}(x, y)}{f_X(x)}$.",
      "<strong>Bona Fide 1D Density:</strong> For fixed $x$, the function $y \\mapsto f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x)$ is a valid density on $\\mathbb{R}$: non-negative and integrates to $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x)\\,dy = 1$.",
      "<strong>Cross-Section Geometry:</strong> Taking a knife slice across the 2D density mountain along $X=x$, dividing by marginal $f_X(x)$ to restore unit area."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x) = \\frac{f_{X,Y}(x, y)}{f_X(x)}, \\quad f_X(x) > 0; \\qquad \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x)\\,dy = 1$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Given that I waited exactly x.</strong> Of the mornings with that wait, you ask how the ride is spread. You slice the joint picture at your wait and rescale the slice so that it has total chance 1.",
    "examTrap": "Borel-Kolmogorov Paradox: conditioning continuous distributions on measure-zero curves g(X,Y)=0 depends on the coordinate parametrization! Slicing is well-defined along coordinate projections.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Conditional density.</b> If $f_X(x)\\gt 0$, the conditional density of $Y$ given $X=x$ is $f_{Y\\mid X}(y\\mid x)=\\dfrac{f_{X,Y}(x,y)}{f_X(x)}$. For each such $x$, $f_{Y\\mid X}(\\cdot\\mid x)$ is a density: $\\int f_{Y\\mid X}(y\\mid x)\\,dy=1$, and $f_{X,Y}(x,y)=f_X(x)f_{Y\\mid X}(y\\mid x)$ (Ross 6.5; Grimmett 4.6).",
    "hint": "You know the wait was exactly x. How do you slice the joint hill to get the law of the ride?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ = the cut through the hill at $x$.</strong> Hold the wait fixed and read the height along the ride direction.",
      "<strong>$f_X(x)$ = the area of that cut.</strong> It is the marginal density of the wait: the total weight of the slice.",
      "<strong>$\\int f_{Y\\mid X}\\,dy=1$ = renormalise.</strong> Dividing the slice by its area turns it into a proper density for the ride, given this wait."
    ],
