    "category": "WORKED BENCHMARK",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Worked Benchmark: Triangular Support & Dependent Marginals",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30706\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"132\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30706)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"16\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30706)\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><polygon points=\"30,108 112,108 112,26\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"88\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f = 2</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y \u2264 x</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"52\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"188\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fX(x) = 2x rises</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"188\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fY(y) = 2(1 \u2212 y) falls</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(y | x) = 1/x on 0 \u2264 y \u2264 x: flat on the slice</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The triangle 0 \u2264 y \u2264 x \u2264 1 with constant density 2. The marginal fX(x) = 2x rises along x, fY(y) = 2(1\u2212y) falls along y, and the slice at x is flat with height 1/x.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem Setup:</strong> Uniform density on triangle $T = \\{(x, y) : 0 \\le y \\le x \\le 1\\}$. Area is $1/2$, so $f_{X,Y}(x, y) = 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{1}_{\\{0 \\le y \\le x \\le 1\\}}$.",
      "<strong>Marginal Integrals:</strong> $f_X(x) = \\int_0^x 2\\,dy = 2x$ on $[0, 1]$. $f_Y(y) = \\int_y^1 2\\,dx = 2(1 - y)$ on $[0, 1]$. Product $f_X f_Y = 4x(1-y) \\ne 2 \\implies X \\not\\perp Y$.",
      "<strong>Conditional Uniformity:</strong> $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x) = \\frac{2}{2x} = \\frac{1}{x} \\mathbf{1}_{\\{0 \\le y \\le x\\}}$, so $Y \\mid X=x \\sim \\text{Uniform}[0, x]$ with $\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X=x] = x/2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{X,Y} = 2, \\quad f_X(x) = 2x, \\quad f_Y(y) = 2(1-y); \\quad f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid x) = \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{0 \\le y \\le x\\}}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A ride cannot exceed its wait.</strong> Suppose, in this toy model, the ride never exceeds the wait and all such pairs are equally likely. Then longer waits are more common, and given the wait, the ride is uniform up to that wait.",
    "examTrap": "Integrating y from 0 to 1 when finding f_X(x)! Because y \u2264 x, integrating past x includes forbidden empty territory, producing an erroneous constant marginal.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Uniform on a triangle.</b> Let $(X,Y)$ have density $f_{X,Y}=2$ on $T=\\{0\\le y\\le x\\le1\\}$ and $0$ elsewhere. Then $f_X(x)=\\int_0^x2\\,dy=2x$ on $[0,1]$, $f_Y(y)=\\int_y^12\\,dx=2(1-y)$ on $[0,1]$, and $f_{Y\\mid X}(y\\mid x)=\\dfrac2{2x}=\\dfrac1x\\mathbf 1_{\\{0\\le y\\le x\\}}$, a uniform law on $[0,x]$. Since $f_{X,Y}\\ne f_Xf_Y$, $X,Y$ are dependent (Ross 6.1).",
    "hint": "Why do the marginals of a flat density on a triangle depend on x and y, and what is the law of y given x?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_X(x)=\\int_0^x2\\,dy=2x$ = the slab at $x$ has height $x$.</strong> Integrating $y$ only from $0$ to $x$ (the triangle's limits) gives a rising line, not a constant.",
      "<strong>$f_Y(y)=2(1-y)$ = the slab at $y$ has length $1-y$.</strong> The marginal of $Y$ falls from $2$ to $0$.",
      "<strong>$f_{Y\\mid X}=1/x$ on $[0,x]$ = flat on the slice.</strong> Given $X=x$, $Y$ is uniform on $[0,x]$, and this depends on $x$, so they are dependent."
    ],
