    "cardNumber": "02",
    "category": "ORDER DENSITIES",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "General Marginal Density of the k-th Order Statistic",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30802\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30802)\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">time</text><circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"52\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"196\" cy=\"70\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"78\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k \u2212 1 below</text><rect x=\"136\" y=\"78\" width=\"78\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n \u2212 k above</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u208d\u2096\u208e at x</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x) = n!/((k\u22121)!(n\u2212k)!) F(x)\u1d4f\u207b\u00b9 [1\u2212F(x)]\u207f\u207b\u1d4f f(x)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">[F(x)]\u1d4f\u207b\u00b9: k\u22121 arrived   [1\u2212F(x)]\u207f\u207b\u1d4f: n\u2212k still to come</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x) dx: the k-th arrives right at x; n!/(\u2026) chooses who</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Six arrival times with the k-th at x: k \u2212 1 sit below it with chance F(x) each, n \u2212 k above with chance 1 \u2212 F(x) each, and the multinomial factor n!/((k\u22121)!(n\u2212k)!) chooses who is who.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Trisection Probability:</strong> Probability that 1 item lies in $[x, x+dx]$ is $f(x)dx$, $(k-1)$ items lie in $(-\\infty, x)$ with probability $F(x)$, and $(n-k)$ items lie in $(x, \\infty)$ with probability $1 - F(x)$.",
      "<strong>Combinatorial Multiplicity:</strong> There are $\\frac{n!}{(k-1)! 1! (n-k)!} = k \\binom{n}{k}$ distinct assignments of the $n$ samples to these three zones.",
      "<strong>General Marginal PDF:</strong> $f_{X_{(k)}}(x) = \\frac{n!}{(k-1)!(n-k)!} [F(x)]^{k-1} [1 - F(x)]^{n-k} f(x)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{X_{(k)}}(x) = \\frac{n!}{(k-1)!(n-k)!} [F(x)]^{k-1} [1 - F(x)]^{n-k} f(x) = k \\binom{n}{k} [F(x)]^{k-1} [1 - F(x)]^{n-k} f(x)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The third bus of five.</strong> For the third of five buses to come at minute $x$, two buses must already be past, one must arrive right at $x$, and two must still be to come. Count the ways to assign roles and multiply the chances.",
    "examTrap": "Forgetting the trailing density factor f(x)! Without f(x), the expression is a discrete binomial probability mass, NOT a continuous probability density function.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Density of the $k$-th order statistic.</b> For i.i.d. $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ with CDF $F$ and density $f$, $f_{X_{(k)}}(x)=\\dfrac{n!}{(k-1)!\\,(n-k)!}[F(x)]^{k-1}[1-F(x)]^{n-k}f(x)=k\\binom nk[F(x)]^{k-1}[1-F(x)]^{n-k}f(x)$ (Ross 6.6; Grimmett 4.14).",
    "hint": "For the k-th bus to arrive exactly at time x, what must the other n \u2212 1 buses be doing?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$[F(x)]^{k-1}$ = $k-1$ buses have already come.</strong> Each of those arrived before $x$, with chance $F(x)$ each.",
      "<strong>$[1-F(x)]^{n-k}$ = $n-k$ buses are still to come.</strong> Each of those is later than $x$, with chance $1-F(x)$ each.",
      "<strong>$\\frac{n!}{(k-1)!(n-k)!}f(x)$ = choose who, and put one exactly at $x$.</strong> The multinomial coefficient picks which bus is the $k$-th, and $f(x)$ is the density of that bus being at $x$. Without it you only have a probability, not a density."
    ],
