    "title": "Exchangeability: Permutation Invariance of Joint Law",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31001\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">days of one commute record, in any order</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 1</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 2</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 3</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 3</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 1</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">day 2</text><line x1=\"58.0\" y1=\"46.0\" x2=\"58.0\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31001)\"/><line x1=\"102.0\" y1=\"46.0\" x2=\"146.0\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31001)\"/><text x=\"189.2\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(X\u2081, X\u2082, X\u2083)</text><text x=\"166.84\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">has the same law as</text><text x=\"189.2\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(X\u2083, X\u2081, X\u2082)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">same joint law for every reshuffling \u03c0: i.i.d. \u2282 exchangeable</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The commute record (X\u2081, X\u2082, X\u2083) and the same record in another order (X\u2083, X\u2081, X\u2082). Exchangeable days have the same joint law under every reshuffling.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> $(X_1, \\dots, X_n)$ is exchangeable if $(X_1, \\dots, X_n) \\stackrel{d}{=} (X_{\\pi(1)}, \\dots, X_{\\pi(n)})$ for every permutation $\\pi \\in S_n$.",
      "<strong>Hierarchy:</strong> $\\text{i.i.d.} \\subsetneq \\text{Exchangeable} \\subsetneq \\text{Identically Distributed}$. Exchangeability is strictly weaker than i.i.d. because mutual dependence is permitted.",
      "<strong>Equi-marginality:</strong> All $X_i$ share identical marginal distributions $F$, and all pairs $(X_i, X_j)$ share identical joint bivariate laws."
    ],
    "math": "$$(X_1, \\dots, X_n) \\stackrel{d}{=} (X_{\\pi(1)}, \\dots, X_{\\pi(n)}) \\quad \\forall \\pi \\in S_n; \\qquad \\text{i.i.d.} \\subset \\text{Exchangeable}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Days with no calendar.</strong> If you hid the dates, you could not tell which day was which, and every ordering of the same record would look equally plausible. The days can still be linked, for example through the same bus company.",
    "examTrap": "Confusing exchangeable with i.i.d.! Exchangeable variables can be strongly correlated (e.g. sampling without replacement from a finite urn).",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Exchangeability.</b> Random variables $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ are exchangeable if $(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)\\overset d=(X_{\\pi(1)},\\ldots,X_{\\pi(n)})$ for every permutation $\\pi$ of $\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$. An infinite sequence is exchangeable if every finite subsequence is. Every i.i.d. sequence is exchangeable, but not conversely (Grimmett 7.2; Durrett 4.1).",
    "hint": "If the order of your commute days carries no information, what does that say about their joint law?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$ = the commute times of days $1$ to $n$.</strong> One list, one joint law for the whole record.",
      "<strong>$(X_{\\pi(1)},\\ldots,X_{\\pi(n)})$ = the same days reshuffled.</strong> Relabel the days by any permutation $\\pi$, for instance by swapping Tuesday and Friday.",
      "<strong>$\\overset d=$ = nothing changes in law.</strong> No day is special: the joint chances are the same for every reshuffling. Independent identical days satisfy it, but dependent days can too."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
