    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31104\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31104)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31104)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"110\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"98\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"102\" cy=\"102\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"114\" cy=\"84\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"90\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"76\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"144\" cy=\"80\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"156\" cy=\"62\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"68\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"54\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"214\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3Y</text><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"84\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3e</text><line x1=\"184\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"184\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"84\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3e = \u03a3Y \u2212 \u03a3YX \u03a3X\u207b\u00b9 \u03a3XY \u2aaf \u03a3Y</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">knowing X removes the explained part of the spread</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The vertical spread \u03a3Y of the rides, and the smaller spread \u03a3e around the regression line. \u03a3e = \u03a3Y \u2212 \u03a3YX \u03a3X\u207b\u00b9 \u03a3XY is what is left after using X.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Matrix Formula:</strong> $\\Sigma_e \\triangleq \\operatorname{Cov}(Y - \\hat{Y}) = \\Sigma_Y - \\Sigma_{YX} \\Sigma_X^{-1} \\Sigma_{XY}$.",
      "<strong>Monotonic Variance Reduction:</strong> Since $\\Sigma_{YX} \\Sigma_X^{-1} \\Sigma_{XY} \\succeq 0$, the error covariance satisfies $\\Sigma_e \\preceq \\Sigma_Y$ (in the Loewner positive semidefinite order). Observation $X$ can only decrease uncertainty.",
      "<strong>Schur Complement Identity:</strong> $\\Sigma_e$ is precisely the Schur complement of block $\\Sigma_X$ in the joint covariance matrix $\\begin{bmatrix} \\Sigma_X & \\Sigma_{XY} \\\\ \\Sigma_{YX} & \\Sigma_Y \\end{bmatrix}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\Sigma_e = \\operatorname{Cov}(Y - \\hat{Y}) = \\Sigma_Y - \\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}\\Sigma_{XY} \\preceq \\Sigma_Y$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>What the phone cannot tell you.</strong> Even with the ETA, some mornings surprise you. The leftover spread is the total spread minus the part the ETA explains.",
    "examTrap": "Singular \u03a3_X: If \u03a3_X is not invertible (observations are linearly redundant), replace \u03a3_X\u207b\u00b9 with the Moore-Penrose pseudoinverse \u03a3_X\u207a.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Error covariance.</b> For the LLSE $\\hat Y$, the error $e=Y-\\hat Y$ has mean $0$ and covariance $\\Sigma_e=\\Sigma_Y-\\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}\\Sigma_{XY}\\preceq\\Sigma_Y$, the Schur complement of $\\Sigma_X$ in the joint covariance (Grimmett 7.9).",
    "hint": "How much of the ride's spread is left after you use the phone's reading?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_Y$ = spread with no information.</strong> The total variation of the ride across mornings.",
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}\\Sigma_{XY}$ = the explained part.</strong> The share of the spread that moves in step with the ETA.",
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_e\\preceq\\Sigma_Y$ = never worse.</strong> What remains is what the signal cannot explain; extra data can only shrink it."
    ],
