    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31203\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"56\" width=\"44\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"52.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><rect x=\"88\" y=\"56\" width=\"70\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"123.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081, X\u2082]</text><rect x=\"170\" y=\"56\" width=\"56\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"198.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081]</text><line x1=\"76.0\" y1=\"67.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31203)\"/><line x1=\"158.0\" y1=\"67.0\" x2=\"170.0\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31203)\"/><text x=\"82\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">know</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">forget X\u2082</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[\ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081, X\u2082] | X\u2081] = \ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081]</text><text x=\"112.24\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">averaging a fine guess back to a coarse guess gives the coarse guess</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[g(X) Y | X] = g(X) \ud835\udd3c[Y | X]: known factors come out</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(what X already tells you is not random any more)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Y, then the finer guess \ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081, X\u2082], then the coarser \ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081]. Forgetting X\u2082 again gives \ud835\udd3c[\ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081, X\u2082] | X\u2081] = \ud835\udd3c[Y | X\u2081].",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Tower Property (Total Expectation):</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]] = \\mathbb{E}[Y]$. The expectation of the conditional expectation recovers the unconditional mean.",
      "<strong>Nested Conditioning:</strong> For nested $\\sigma$-algebras $\\mathcal{G}_1 \\subset \\mathcal{G}_2$, $\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid \\mathcal{G}_2] \\mid \\mathcal{G}_1] = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid \\mathcal{G}_1]$. Conditioning on less information always wins.",
      "<strong>Taking Out What Is Known:</strong> If $g(X)$ is $\\sigma(X)$-measurable, $\\mathbb{E}[g(X) Y \\mid X] = g(X)\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]$. Known variables act as scalars inside the conditional expectation."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}\\left[\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X_1, X_2] \\;\\middle|\\; X_1\\right] = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X_1], \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[g(X) Y \\mid X] = g(X) \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Refine, then coarsen.</strong> Averaging your detailed forecast (ETA and weather) over the weather you do not know brings you back to the forecast from the ETA alone.",
    "examTrap": "Reversing the tower ordering: E[E[Y|X\u2081]|X\u2081, X\u2082] = E[Y|X\u2081], NOT E[Y|X\u2081, X\u2082]! Finer conditioning cannot invent new information that was already lost.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Tower property and taking out what is known.</b> For $\\sigma$-algebras $\\mathcal G\\subset\\mathcal H$: $\\mathbb E[\\mathbb E[Y\\mid\\mathcal H]\\mid\\mathcal G]=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid\\mathcal G]$, in particular $\\mathbb E[\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X_1,X_2]\\mid X_1]=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X_1]$. Also $\\mathbb E[g(X)Y\\mid X]=g(X)\\,\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ (Ross 7.5; Grimmett 3.7).",
    "hint": "If you refine a guess with extra information and then forget it again, what do you get back?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X_1,X_2]$ = the finer guess.</strong> The average ride given both the ETA and the weather.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[\\cdot\\mid X_1]$ = then forget the weather.</strong> Averaging the finer guess over what $X_1$ does not fix lands on the coarser guess.",
      "<strong>$g(X)\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ = known factors come out.</strong> Given $X$, $g(X)$ is not random, so it passes through the average."
    ],
