    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "MMSE vs LLSE: Non-Linearity & Superiority",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31205\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31205)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31205)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"54.58\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"59.1712\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"41.4088\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"49.2928\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"34.8232\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"46.0\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"34.8232\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"138\" cy=\"49.2928\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"152\" cy=\"41.4088\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"59.1712\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"54.58\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"194\" cy=\"75.6352\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"36\" y1=\"97.28\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"77.6\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M36.0,63.0 L39.3,61.0 L42.6,59.1 L45.8,57.3 L49.1,55.6 L52.4,53.9 L55.7,52.4 L59.0,50.9 L62.2,49.6 L65.5,48.3 L68.8,47.1 L72.1,46.0 L75.4,45.0 L78.6,44.1 L81.9,43.3 L85.2,42.6 L88.5,41.9 L91.8,41.4 L95.0,40.9 L98.3,40.6 L101.6,40.3 L104.9,40.1 L108.2,40.0 L111.4,40.0 L114.7,40.1 L118.0,40.3 L121.3,40.5 L124.6,40.9 L127.8,41.3 L131.1,41.9 L134.4,42.5 L137.7,43.2 L141.0,44.0 L144.2,44.9 L147.5,45.9 L150.8,47.0 L154.1,48.2 L157.4,49.4 L160.6,50.8 L163.9,52.2 L167.2,53.7 L170.5,55.4 L173.8,57.1 L177.0,58.9 L180.3,60.8 L183.6,62.8 L186.9,64.8 L190.2,67.0 L193.4,69.2 L196.7,71.6 L200.0,74.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X] curve</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">LLSE line</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c(Y \u2212 \ud835\udd3c[Y | X])\u00b2 \u2264 \ud835\udd3c(Y \u2212 \u0176)\u00b2 \u2264 Var(Y)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Data around a curved relationship, the best curve \ud835\udd3c[Y | X] and the straight LLSE line (dashed). The curve's error is smaller, which in turn is at most Var(Y).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Performance Ordering:</strong> $\\text{MMSE Error} = \\mathbb{E}[(Y - \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X])^2] \\le \\text{LLSE Error} \\le \\operatorname{Var}(Y)$.",
      "<strong>Extreme Non-Linear Gap:</strong> When $Y = X^2$ with symmetric $X$, $\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) = 0$. LLSE outputs a useless flat line $\\hat{Y} = \\mathbb{E}[Y]$, while MMSE outputs exact parabola $\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X] = X^2$ with zero error!",
      "<strong>Coincidence Theorem:</strong> MMSE and LLSE are IDENTICAL if and only if $\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]$ is an affine function of $X$ (which holds automatically for jointly Gaussian systems)."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}\\left[\\left(Y - \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]\\right)^2\\right] \\le \\mathbb{E}\\left[\\left(Y - \\hat{Y}_{\\text{LLSE}}\\right)^2\\right] \\le \\operatorname{Var}(Y)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Line versus curve.</strong> If the ETA matters in a curved way, say it is useless until it gets large, a straight-line rule loses to the curve. If the link is straight, the two give the same guess.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming LLSE is always a close approximation to MMSE. In non-linear symmetric systems, LLSE has 0% predictive power while MMSE has 100% predictive accuracy.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>MMSE versus LLSE.</b> For $\\mathbb E[Y^2]\\lt \\infty$, $\\mathbb E[(Y-\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X])^2]\\le\\mathbb E[(Y-\\hat Y_{\\rm LLSE})^2]\\le\\operatorname{Var}(Y)$, since the linear estimators are a subset of all functions of $X$ and constants are a subset of linear ones. They coincide iff $\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ is affine in $X$, e.g. jointly Gaussian $(X,Y)$ (Grimmett 7.9).",
    "hint": "When does a straight-line guess lose to the curve of slice averages, and when do they agree?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[(Y-\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X])^2]$ = error of the best curve.</strong> The smallest error over all functions of $X$.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[(Y-\\hat Y_{\\rm LLSE})^2]$ = error of the best line.</strong> Larger or equal, since lines are a smaller family to choose from.",
      "<strong>$\\le\\operatorname{Var}(Y)$ = never worse than ignoring $X$.</strong> The constant guess $\\mu_Y$ is itself a linear estimator."
    ],
