    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Multivariate Gaussian PDF & The Mahalanobis Form",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31301\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31301)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31301)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><ellipse cx=\"86\" cy=\"62\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" transform=\"rotate(-30 86 62)\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"62\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc</text><line x1=\"86.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"118.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31301)\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x) = exp(\u2212\u00bd d\u00b2)</text><text x=\"148.64\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">/ ((2\u03c0)^(n/2) |\u03a3|^(1/2))</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">d\u00b2 = Mahalanobis</text><text x=\"155.92000000000002\" y=\"81\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">distance: spread-aware</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3 \u227b 0 needed</text><text x=\"105.87\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the outline of the cloud of (ETA error, ride error) mornings; \u03bc is its centre</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The outline of the cloud of mornings around its centre \u03bc. The density falls with the Mahalanobis distance d\u00b2 = (x \u2212 \u03bc)\u1d40\u03a3\u207b\u00b9(x \u2212 \u03bc), measured in the cloud's own shape.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Density Formula:</strong> For non-singular $\\Sigma \\succ 0$, $f_{\\mathbf{X}}(\\mathbf{x}) = \\frac{1}{(2\\pi)^{n/2} |\\Sigma|^{1/2}} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu})^\\top \\Sigma^{-1} (\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu})\\right)$ on $\\mathbb{R}^n$.",
      "<strong>Mahalanobis Distance:</strong> Level sets of constant probability density are ellipsoids defined by quadratic form $d_M^2(\\mathbf{x}, \\boldsymbol{\\mu}) = (\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu})^\\top \\Sigma^{-1} (\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu}) = c^2$.",
      "<strong>Eigenvector Geometry:</strong> Principal axes align with eigenvectors $v_i$ of $\\Sigma$, with half-lengths proportional to standard deviations $\\sqrt{\\lambda_i}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{\\mathbf{X}}(\\mathbf{x}) = \\frac{1}{(2\\pi)^{n/2} |\\Sigma|^{1/2}} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu})^\\top \\Sigma^{-1}(\\mathbf{x} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu})\\right), \\quad \\Sigma \\succ 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A cloud shaped by \u03a3.</strong> Mornings scatter around the typical one in an oval. A point far along the long axis of the oval counts as close; the same distance across it counts as far.",
    "examTrap": "Attempting to write density when |\u03a3| = 0 (singular covariance). When variables are linearly dependent, the distribution is degenerate and has no density with respect to Lebesgue measure on \u211d\u207f.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Multivariate normal density.</b> $X\\in\\mathbb R^n$ is $\\mathcal N(\\mu,\\Sigma)$ with $\\Sigma\\succ0$ if it has density $f_X(x)=\\dfrac{1}{(2\\pi)^{n/2}|\\Sigma|^{1/2}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\tfrac12(x-\\mu)^\\top\\Sigma^{-1}(x-\\mu)\\right)$ (Ross 7.8; Grimmett 4.9).",
    "hint": "How does a bell curve in many dimensions know the spread and the tilt of the cloud?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mu$ = the centre of the cloud.</strong> The average (ETA error, ride error) over mornings; the density peaks there.",
      "<strong>$(x-\\mu)^\\top\\Sigma^{-1}(x-\\mu)$ = squared Mahalanobis distance.</strong> Distance from the centre measured in the cloud's own spread and tilt, so tilted stretches count as short.",
      "<strong>$(2\\pi)^{n/2}|\\Sigma|^{1/2}$ = the normaliser.</strong> It makes the total volume 1; a larger cloud (bigger $|\\Sigma|$) means a lower peak."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
