    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Worked Benchmark: Marginally Normal \u2260 Jointly Normal (Y = S \u00b7 X)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31306\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31306)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"10\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31306)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"10\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"90\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"80\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"66\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"46\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"34\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"32\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"42\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"56\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"76\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"94\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y = S\u00b7X</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">S = \u00b11 coin</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">X + Y = 0</text><text x=\"188.68\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">half the time</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X, Y each \ud835\udca9(0,1) and Cov = 0, yet \u2119(X + Y = 0) = \u00bd:</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">not jointly Gaussian, so uncorrelated \u2260 independent</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Points (X, Y = SX) lie on the two diagonals instead of an oval cloud. Both X and Y are \ud835\udca9(0,1) with Cov = 0, but \u2119(X + Y = 0) = \u00bd, so the pair is not jointly Gaussian.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Setup:</strong> Let $X \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$ and let $S \\in \\{-1, +1\\}$ with $\\mathbb{P}(S = 1) = \\mathbb{P}(S = -1) = 1/2$ independently of $X$. Define $Y = S \\cdot X$.",
      "<strong>Marginal Normality & Zero Covariance:</strong> By symmetry, $Y \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$ and $\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) = \\mathbb{E}[S X^2] = \\mathbb{E}[S]\\mathbb{E}[X^2] = 0(1) = 0$.",
      "<strong>Non-Gaussian Joint Law:</strong> The sum $X + Y = X(1 + S)$ equals $2X$ with probability $1/2$, and equals $0$ with probability $1/2$. It has atom $\\mathbb{P}(X + Y = 0) = 1/2$, so $X+Y$ is NOT normal $\\implies (X, Y)$ is NOT jointly Gaussian!"
    ],
    "math": "$$X, Y \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, 1), \\quad \\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) = 0, \\quad \\text{yet } \\mathbb{P}(X + Y = 0) = \\tfrac{1}{2} \\implies (X, Y) \\text{ NOT jointly Gaussian!}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Each bell, but a cross, not an oval.</strong> The phone error and the ride error are each bell-shaped, but their pairs lie on the two diagonals instead of in a cloud, because a coin flip fixes the sign.",
    "examTrap": "Concluding independence because Cov(X, Y) = 0! They are uncorrelated, but |Y| = |X| (complete deterministic dependence). Joint normality is strictly required for uncorrelated \u21d4 independent.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Normal marginals, not jointly normal.</b> Let $X\\sim\\mathcal N(0,1)$, $S=\\pm1$ with probability $\\tfrac12$ each, independent of $X$, and $Y=SX$. Then $Y\\sim\\mathcal N(0,1)$ and $\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)=\\mathbb E[S]\\mathbb E[X^2]=0$, but $\\mathbb P(X+Y=0)=\\mathbb P(S=-1)=\\tfrac12$, so $X+Y$ is not normal (a normal law has no atoms): $(X,Y)$ is not jointly Gaussian and $X,Y$ are dependent (Ross 7.8; Grimmett 4.9).",
    "hint": "Can two bell-shaped variables with zero covariance still be dependent?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Y=SX$ = flip the sign at random.</strong> With a fair coin $S$, $Y$ is $X$ or $-X$, which is again a standard normal.",
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)=0$ = no straight-line link.</strong> The coin makes the covariance average to zero.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X+Y=0)=\\tfrac12$ = a weighted total with an atom.</strong> A jointly Gaussian pair would make $X+Y$ normal, with no atoms, so the pair is not jointly Gaussian."
    ],
