    "category": "RANDOM SUMS",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Random Sums S_N = \u2211_{i=1}^N X_i & Stopping Times",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31401\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"52\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2081</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"52\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"86\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2082</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"52\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2083</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"52\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2084</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"52\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2085</text><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N = 4 stops this morning (random)</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">not reached</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S = \u2211 X\u1d62 1{N \u2265 i}</text><text x=\"115.776\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">{N \u2265 i} is decided before stop i: the indicator is independent of X\u1d62</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(N is a stopping time)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "N = 4 stops are reached this morning, each adding a delay X\u1d62; X\u2085 is not reached. S = \u2211 X\u1d62 1{N \u2265 i}, and the switch 1{N \u2265 i} is independent of X\u1d62.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Random Sum Formulation:</strong> For i.i.d. $X_i$ with mean $\\mu$ and variance $\\sigma^2$, $S_N = \\sum_{i=1}^N X_i$ sums a random integer number of terms $N \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$.",
      "<strong>Stopping Time Condition:</strong> $N$ is a stopping time with respect to filtration $\\mathcal{F}_n = \\sigma(X_1, \\dots, X_n)$ if $\\{N = n\\} \\in \\mathcal{F}_n$ for all $n$ (halting rule does NOT depend on future outcomes).",
      "<strong>Indicator Independence:</strong> $S_N = \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty X_i \\mathbf{1}_{\\{N \\ge i\\}}$. Crucially, event $\\{N \\ge i\\} = \\{N \\le i-1\\}^c$ depends only on $X_1, \\dots, X_{i-1}$, and is therefore independent of $X_i$."
    ],
    "math": "$$S_N = \\sum_{i=1}^N X_i = \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty X_i\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{N \\ge i\\}}, \\qquad \\{N \\ge i\\} \\in \\sigma(X_1, \\dots, X_{i-1}) \\implies \\mathbf{1}_{\\{N \\ge i\\}} \\perp X_i$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A route with a random number of stops.</strong> You ride until something happens: you reach campus, or the bus breaks. Whether you board stop $i$ is decided by what happened earlier, not by that stop's own delay.",
    "examTrap": "Applying Wald's identities when N looks into the future! For example, N = argmax_{1 \u2264 i \u2264 5} X_i depends on future terms; Wald's equation fails completely for anticipatory stopping rules.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Random sums.</b> Let $X_1,X_2,\\ldots$ be i.i.d. and $N\\ge0$ integer-valued. The random sum is $S_N=\\sum_{i=1}^NX_i=\\sum_{i=1}^\\infty X_i\\mathbf 1_{\\{N\\ge i\\}}$. If $N$ is a stopping time ($\\{N\\ge i\\}\\in\\sigma(X_1,\\ldots,X_{i-1})$) or independent of $(X_i)$, then $\\mathbf 1_{\\{N\\ge i\\}}$ is independent of $X_i$ (Ross 7.5; Grimmett 5.1).",
    "hint": "If the number of stops is itself random, when can you still treat each stop's delay as separate from whether it is reached?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$S_N=\\sum_{i=1}^NX_i$ = total delay over $N$ stops.</strong> Both the number of terms and each term are random.",
      "<strong>$\\sum X_i\\mathbf 1_{\\{N\\ge i\\}}$ = switch each stop on or off.</strong> Stop $i$ contributes only if you get at least that far; this turns it into an infinite sum with fixed length.",
      "<strong>$\\{N\\ge i\\}\\in\\sigma(X_1,\\ldots,X_{i-1})$ = decided before stop $i$.</strong> Whether you reach stop $i$ depends only on earlier delays, so the switch is independent of $X_i$."
    ],
