    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31504\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31504)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31504)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9 \u2208 [0,1]</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2099(\u03c9)</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"92\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 1</text><rect x=\"76\" y=\"72\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"40\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 2</text><rect x=\"122\" y=\"52\" width=\"13.333333333333334\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"142\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 3</text><rect x=\"168\" y=\"32\" width=\"10.0\" height=\"80\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"188\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 4</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">spike of height n\u00b2 on [0, 1/n]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">any fixed \u03c9 ends up outside the spike: X\u2099(\u03c9) \u2192 0 a.s.</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">but \ud835\udd3c|X\u2099| = n</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2192 \u221e: no L\u00b9 limit</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Spikes of height n\u00b2 on [0, 1/n] for n = 1, 2, 3, 4. Any fixed \u03c9 escapes eventually (X\u2099 \u2192 0 a.s.), but the area under each spike is n, so \ud835\udd3c|X\u2099| \u2192 \u221e.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Spike Construction:</strong> Let $\\mathbb{P}(X_n = n^2) = 1/n$ and $\\mathbb{P}(X_n = 0) = 1 - 1/n$.",
      "<strong>Almost Sure Zero:</strong> By Borel-Cantelli (using independent trials with $\\sum 1/n^2 \\lt  \\infty$), for almost every $\\omega$, $X_n(\\omega) = 0$ for all sufficiently large $n$, so $X_n \\xrightarrow{a.s.} 0$.",
      "<strong>$L^1$ Mean Explosion:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[|X_n|] = n^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{n} = n \\to \\infty$. The expectation explodes to infinity even though the variable is zero almost surely!"
    ],
    "math": "$$X_n(\\omega) \\to 0 \\text{ a.s.}, \\quad \\text{yet } \\mathbb{E}[|X_n|] = n \\to \\infty \\implies X_n \\not\\xrightarrow{L^1} 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Rare catastrophes.</strong> Each morning you will eventually stop seeing the disaster, but the disaster gets so extreme when it does strike that its contribution to the average grows without bound.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming almost sure convergence allows exchanging limit and expectation: lim E[X_n] = E[lim X_n] strictly requires Uniform Integrability or a Dominated Bound (DCT).",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Escaping spike.</b> On $[0,1]$ with Lebesgue measure let $X_n=n^2\\mathbf 1_{(0,1/n)}$. For each fixed $\\omega$, $X_n(\\omega)=0$ once $n\\gt 1/\\omega$, so $X_n\\to0$ a.s., but $\\mathbb E|X_n|=n^2\\cdot\\frac1n=n\\to\\infty$, so $X_n\\not\\to0$ in $L^1$ (Grimmett 7.2; Durrett 2.3).",
    "hint": "Can every single run settle to zero while the average size of the miss blows up?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$X_n=n^2\\mathbf 1_{(0,1/n)}$ = a tall spike on a thin window.</strong> Height $n^2$ on the first $1/n$ of the mornings, zero elsewhere.",
      "<strong>$X_n(\\omega)=0$ for $n\\gt 1/\\omega$ = every run escapes the spike.</strong> The window shrinks to zero length, so each fixed $\\omega$ falls outside it eventually: a.s. convergence to 0.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E|X_n|=n\\to\\infty$ = the area grows.</strong> Height times width is $n^2\\cdot\\frac1n=n$: a rare, huge delay dominates the average."
    ],
