    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31603\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31603)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31603)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(A\u2099)</text><rect x=\"34\" y=\"40.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"60.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"52\" y=\"70.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"30.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"80.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"20.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"88\" y=\"85.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"15.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"106\" y=\"88.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"12.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"124\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"10.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"91.42857142857143\" width=\"12\" height=\"8.571428571428571\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"160\" y=\"92.5\" width=\"12\" height=\"7.5\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"178\" y=\"93.33333333333333\" width=\"12\" height=\"6.666666666666667\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"196\" y=\"94.0\" width=\"12\" height=\"6.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M34.0,100.0 L38.5,92.0 L43.0,85.4 L47.5,79.9 L52.0,75.0 L56.5,70.8 L61.0,67.0 L65.5,63.6 L70.0,60.4 L74.5,57.6 L79.0,54.9 L83.5,52.4 L88.0,50.1 L92.5,47.9 L97.0,45.9 L101.5,43.9 L106.0,42.1 L110.5,40.3 L115.0,38.6 L119.5,37.0 L124.0,35.5 L128.5,34.0 L133.0,32.6 L137.5,31.3 L142.0,29.9 L146.5,28.7 L151.0,27.5 L155.5,26.3 L160.0,25.1 L164.5,24.0 L169.0,23.0 L173.5,21.9 L178.0,20.9 L182.5,19.9 L187.0,19.0 L191.5,18.0 L196.0,17.1 L200.5,16.2 L205.0,15.4 L209.5,14.5 L214.0,13.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">independent days, \u2211 \u2119(A\u2099) = \u221e (chances like 1/n)</text><text x=\"115.88\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2211 diverges (dashed: running total keeps rising) \u21d2 \u2119(late i.o.) = 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">independence is essential here</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Bars of \u2119(A\u2099) = 1/n and, dashed, the running total \u2211\u2119(A\u2096), which keeps rising without bound. With independence this forces \u2119(A\u2099 i.o.) = 1.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Theorem Statement:</strong> If events $\\{A_n\\}$ are MUTUALLY INDEPENDENT and $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(A_n) = \\infty$, then $\\mathbb{P}(\\limsup A_n) = \\mathbb{P}(A_n \\text{ i.o.}) = 1$.",
      "<strong>Product Inequality Proof:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(\\bigcap_{k=n}^m A_k^c) = \\prod_{k=n}^m (1 - \\mathbb{P}(A_k)) \\le \\prod_{k=n}^m e^{-\\mathbb{P}(A_k)} = \\exp(-\\sum_{k=n}^m \\mathbb{P}(A_k)) \\to 0$. Thus $\\mathbb{P}(\\bigcup_{k=n}^\\infty A_k) = 1$ for all $n$.",
      "<strong>Strict Independence Mandate:</strong> Unlike BC1, BC2 FAILS without independence! Correlated events with divergent sums can fail to occur infinitely often."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\{A_n\\} \\text{ independent}, \\quad \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(A_n) = \\infty \\implies \\mathbb{P}\\left(\\limsup_{n \\to \\infty} A_n\\right) = 1$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Bad luck that never quite fades.</strong> If the chance of an incident on day $n$ is $1/n$ and days are independent, you can be certain that incidents never stop, though they become rarer.",
    "examTrap": "Applying BC2 without independence! If A_n = A for all n with P(A) = 1/2, then \u2211 P(A_n) = \u221e, yet P(A_n i.o.) = P(A) = 1/2 \u2260 1! Independence is indispensable.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Second Borel\u2013Cantelli lemma.</b> If $A_1,A_2,\\ldots$ are independent and $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty\\mathbb P(A_n)=\\infty$, then $\\mathbb P(A_n\\text{ i.o.})=1$. Proof: $\\mathbb P(\\bigcap_{k\\ge n}A_k^c)=\\prod_{k\\ge n}(1-\\mathbb P(A_k))\\le\\exp(-\\sum_{k\\ge n}\\mathbb P(A_k))=0$ (Grimmett 7.3; Ross 8.2).",
    "hint": "If days are independent and the chances of being late never add up to a finite number, how often are you late?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\{A_n\\}$ independent = days are unrelated.</strong> This is essential: without it, correlated days can make the conclusion fail.",
      "<strong>$\\sum\\mathbb P(A_n)=\\infty$ = the chances add up to infinity.</strong> Chances like $1/n$ shrink, but not fast enough: the running total keeps rising.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(\\limsup A_n)=1$ = late infinitely often, for sure.</strong> The chance of never being late again from day $n$ on is $\\prod(1-p_k)\\le e^{-\\sum p_k}=0$."
    ],
