    "title": "Kolmogorov\u2019s Zero-One Law: Binary Tail Probabilities",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31604\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31604)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31604)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">days</text><rect x=\"24\" y=\"40\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">first k days:</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">no effect</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"40\" width=\"140\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">tail event E:</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">depends only on the far future</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udcaf = \u22c2\u2099 \u03c3(X\u2099, X\u2099\u208a\u2081, \u2026)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">E \u2208 \ud835\udcaf: unchanged by altering any finite number of days</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">independent days \u21d2 \u2119(E) = 0 or 1, never in between</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">e.g. \u201cthe long-run average exists\u201d: all or nothing</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The first k days (shaded) cannot affect a tail event E, which depends only on the far future. For independent days, every such event has chance 0 or 1.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Tail $\\sigma$-Algebra:</strong> $\\mathcal{T} \\triangleq \\bigcap_{n=1}^\\infty \\sigma(X_n, X_{n+1}, \\dots)$. An event $E \\in \\mathcal{T}$ is unaffected by changing the values of any finite prefix $X_1, \\dots, X_M$.",
      "<strong>Kolmogorov's Theorem:</strong> If $\\{X_n\\}$ are independent, then for every tail event $E \\in \\mathcal{T}$, $\\mathbb{P}(E) \\in \\{0, 1\\}$. Tail probabilities are binary: either impossible or certain!",
      "<strong>Canonical Tail Events:</strong> Event $\\{\\sum X_n \\text{ converges}\\}$, $\\{\\lim X_n \\text{ exists}\\}$, $\\{\\limsup X_n \\le c\\}$, and $\\{\\lim \\frac{1}{n}\\sum X_i = \\mu\\}$ are all tail events."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathcal{T} = \\bigcap_{n=1}^\\infty \\sigma(X_n, X_{n+1}, \\dots), \\quad \\{X_n\\} \\text{ independent} \\implies \\mathbb{P}(E) \\in \\{0, 1\\} \\quad \\forall E \\in \\mathcal{T}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The far future is all or nothing.</strong> Whether your long-run average commute settles down cannot depend on any finite number of days, so for independent days it either happens for sure or never happens.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming event {X\u2081 = 1} is a tail event! The first step X\u2081 is in the prefix, not the tail. Only asymptotic properties invariant to finite prefixes belong to \ud835\udcaf.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Kolmogorov's zero\u2013one law.</b> Let $X_1,X_2,\\ldots$ be independent and $\\mathcal T=\\bigcap_{n=1}^\\infty\\sigma(X_n,X_{n+1},\\ldots)$ the tail $\\sigma$-algebra. Then $\\mathbb P(E)\\in\\{0,1\\}$ for every $E\\in\\mathcal T$ (Grimmett 7.3; Durrett 2.5).",
    "hint": "For independent days, which events are decided only by the far future, and what are their possible chances?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sigma(X_n,X_{n+1},\\ldots)$ = what the days from $n$ on can tell you.</strong> Questions about the record from day $n$ forward.",
      "<strong>$\\bigcap_n$ = questions that survive dropping any finite number of days.</strong> A tail event does not change if you alter the first $k$ days, for any $k$.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(E)\\in\\{0,1\\}$ = all or nothing.</strong> For independent days, a question about the far future is either certain or impossible; for example \u201cthe long-run average exists\u201d."
    ],
