    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31902\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"40.0\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">i</text><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"36.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"90.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k\u2032</text><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">j</text><line x1=\"50.0\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"109.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31902)\"/><line x1=\"50.0\" y1=\"64.0\" x2=\"109.0\" y2=\"86.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31902)\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"39.0\" x2=\"190.0\" y2=\"56.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31902)\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"87.0\" x2=\"190.0\" y2=\"64.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31902)\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">m steps</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n steps</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pass through some middle state k</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u1d62\u2c7c\u207d\u1d50\u207a\u207f\u207e = \u2211\u2096 P\u1d62\u2096\u207d\u1d50\u207e P\u2096\u2c7c\u207d\u207f\u207e  \u21d4  P\u207d\u1d50\u207a\u207f\u207e = P\u1d50 P\u207f</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p\u207d\u207f\u207e = p\u207d\u2070\u207e P\u207f: n-day distribution</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "To go from i to j in m + n steps, pass through some state k after m steps and sum over all k. This is the matrix product P\u1d50\u207a\u207f = P\u1d50 P\u207f.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Intermediate Splitting:</strong> To transition from $i$ to $j$ in $(m+n)$ steps, the chain must pass through some intermediate state $k$ at step $m$.",
      "<strong>Chapman-Kolmogorov Formula:</strong> $P_{ij}^{(m+n)} = \\sum_{k \\in S} P_{ik}^{(m)} P_{kj}^{(n)}$ for all $m, n \\ge 1$.",
      "<strong>Matrix Power Representation:</strong> In matrix form, $P^{(n)} = P^n$. Unconditional distribution after $n$ steps is $\\mathbf{p}^{(n)} = \\mathbf{p}^{(0)} P^n$ (where $\\mathbf{p}^{(0)}$ is a row vector)."
    ],
    "math": "$$P_{ij}^{(m+n)} = \\sum_{k \\in S} P_{ik}^{(m)} P_{kj}^{(n)} \\iff P^{(m+n)} = P^m P^n, \\qquad \\mathbf{p}^{(n)} = \\mathbf{p}^{(0)} P^n$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two weeks ahead by squaring.</strong> To predict the day after tomorrow, sum over what tomorrow could be: on time, late or cancelled. That sum is exactly one matrix product, so $n$ days ahead is the $n$-th power of the table.",
    "examTrap": "Multiplying state distribution from the wrong side: p^{(n)} = p^{(0)} P^n where p^{(0)} is a ROW vector. Writing P^n p^{(0)} causes matrix dimension mismatch!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Chapman\u2013Kolmogorov.</b> For a Markov chain, $P^{(m+n)}_{ij}=\\sum_{k\\in S}P^{(m)}_{ik}P^{(n)}_{kj}$, i.e. $P^{(m+n)}=P^mP^n$ and so $P^{(n)}=P^n$. If $\\mathbf p^{(0)}$ is the law of $X_0$, then $\\mathbf p^{(n)}=\\mathbf p^{(0)}P^n$ is the law of $X_n$ (Ross 4.2; Grimmett 6.1).",
    "hint": "How do you get the chances for n days ahead from the one-day table?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$P^{(m+n)}_{ij}$ = from $i$ to $j$ in $m+n$ days.</strong> The chance of being in $j$ after $m+n$ steps, started at $i$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_kP^{(m)}_{ik}P^{(n)}_{kj}$ = pass through a middle state.</strong> After $m$ days you are at some $k$; sum over every possible $k$, then continue for $n$ days.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbf p^{(n)}=\\mathbf p^{(0)}P^n$ = the law after $n$ days.</strong> Multiply the starting row vector by the matrix $n$ times."
    ],
