    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31904\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31904)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31904)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u1d62\u1d62\u207d\u207f\u207e</text><path d=\"M30.0,70.4 L33.8,72.7 L37.6,74.6 L41.4,76.3 L45.2,77.8 L49.0,79.1 L52.8,80.2 L56.6,81.3 L60.4,82.2 L64.2,83.0 L68.0,83.8 L71.8,84.5 L75.6,85.2 L79.4,85.7 L83.2,86.3 L87.0,86.8 L90.8,87.3 L94.6,87.7 L98.4,88.1 L102.2,88.5 L106.0,88.9 L109.8,89.2 L113.6,89.5 L117.4,89.8 L121.2,90.1 L125.0,90.4 L128.8,90.6 L132.6,90.8 L136.4,91.1 L140.2,91.3 L144.0,91.5 L147.8,91.7 L151.6,91.9 L155.4,92.1 L159.2,92.2 L163.0,92.4 L166.8,92.6 L170.6,92.7 L174.4,92.9 L178.2,93.0 L182.0,93.1 L185.8,93.3 L189.6,93.4 L193.4,93.5 L197.2,93.6 L201.0,93.7 L204.8,93.8 L208.6,93.9 L212.4,94.0 L216.2,94.1 L220.0,94.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">recurrent: \u2211 diverges</text><path d=\"M30.0,72.6 L33.8,76.0 L37.6,79.1 L41.4,81.7 L45.2,84.1 L49.0,86.1 L52.8,87.8 L56.6,89.4 L60.4,90.7 L64.2,91.9 L68.0,92.9 L71.8,93.8 L75.6,94.6 L79.4,95.3 L83.2,95.9 L87.0,96.4 L90.8,96.9 L94.6,97.3 L98.4,97.6 L102.2,97.9 L106.0,98.2 L109.8,98.4 L113.6,98.6 L117.4,98.8 L121.2,98.9 L125.0,99.1 L128.8,99.2 L132.6,99.3 L136.4,99.4 L140.2,99.5 L144.0,99.5 L147.8,99.6 L151.6,99.6 L155.4,99.7 L159.2,99.7 L163.0,99.8 L166.8,99.8 L170.6,99.8 L174.4,99.8 L178.2,99.9 L182.0,99.9 L185.8,99.9 L189.6,99.9 L193.4,99.9 L197.2,99.9 L201.0,99.9 L204.8,99.9 L208.6,100.0 L212.4,100.0 L216.2,100.0 L220.0,100.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">transient: \u2211 converges</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f = \u2119(ever return to i)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">recurrent \u21d4 f\u1d62\u1d62 = 1 \u21d4 \u2211\u2099 P\u1d62\u1d62\u207d\u207f\u207e = \u221e</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">transient \u21d4 f\u1d62\u1d62 &lt; 1 \u21d4 \u2211\u2099 P\u1d62\u1d62\u207d\u207f\u207e &lt; \u221e</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Return chances P\u1d62\u1d62\u207d\u207f\u207e against n. For a recurrent state they decay slowly enough to sum to infinity; for a transient state they decay fast and the sum is finite.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>First Return Probability:</strong> Let $\\tau_i \\triangleq \\min\\{n \\ge 1 : X_n = i\\}$. Return probability is $f_{ii} \\triangleq \\mathbb{P}(\\tau_i \\lt  \\infty \\mid X_0 = i)$.",
      "<strong>Recurrent ($f_{ii} = 1$):</strong> Returns to state $i$ with probability 1; the chain visits state $i$ infinitely many times almost surely, so $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty P_{ii}^{(n)} = \\infty$.",
      "<strong>Transient ($f_{ii} \\lt  1$):</strong> Non-zero probability $(1 - f_{ii})$ of never returning; total return visits follow $\\text{Geometric}(1 - f_{ii})$ with finite expectation $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty P_{ii}^{(n)} = \\frac{f_{ii}}{1 - f_{ii}} \\lt  \\infty$."
    ],
    "math": "$$i \\text{ recurrent} \\iff f_{ii} = 1 \\iff \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty P_{ii}^{(n)} = \\infty; \\qquad i \\text{ transient} \\iff f_{ii} \\lt  1 \\iff \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty P_{ii}^{(n)} \\lt  \\infty$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A normal morning keeps coming back.</strong> A usual on-time morning recurs for ever. But a one-off, like the bus route being scrapped, may happen once and never again, and that state is transient.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming all states in a finite Markov chain can be transient. In ANY finite-state Markov chain, at least ONE state must be recurrent (probability mass has nowhere to escape).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Recurrence and transience.</b> Let $f_{ii}=\\mathbb P(X_n=i\\text{ for some }n\\ge1\\mid X_0=i)$. State $i$ is recurrent iff $f_{ii}=1$ iff $\\sum_{n\\ge1}P^{(n)}_{ii}=\\infty$, and transient iff $f_{ii}\\lt 1$ iff $\\sum_{n\\ge1}P^{(n)}_{ii}\\lt \\infty$ (Ross 4.3; Grimmett 6.2).",
    "hint": "Will you return to the same kind of morning for sure, or may you leave and never come back?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_{ii}$ = the chance of ever returning to $i$.</strong> Start at $i$; $f_{ii}$ is the probability of being at $i$ again at some later day.",
      "<strong>$f_{ii}=1$ = recurrent.</strong> You return for sure, hence infinitely often, so the expected number of visits $\\sum_nP^{(n)}_{ii}$ is infinite.",
      "<strong>$f_{ii}\\lt 1$ = transient.</strong> Each visit may be the last; the number of visits is geometric, so $\\sum_nP^{(n)}_{ii}\\lt \\infty$."
    ],
