    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32003\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32003)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32003)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">i</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"71.33874757704842\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"79.46331523869631\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"85.2848223531423\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"89.45611447537092\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"92.44497588649753\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"94.58658867053549\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"96.1211212854238\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M40.0,60.0 L44.2,62.3 L48.4,64.4 L52.6,66.4 L56.8,68.3 L61.0,70.1 L65.2,71.8 L69.4,73.4 L73.6,74.9 L77.8,76.3 L82.0,77.7 L86.2,78.9 L90.4,80.1 L94.6,81.3 L98.8,82.3 L103.0,83.3 L107.2,84.3 L111.4,85.2 L115.6,86.0 L119.8,86.8 L124.0,87.5 L128.2,88.2 L132.4,88.9 L136.6,89.5 L140.8,90.1 L145.0,90.7 L149.2,91.2 L153.4,91.7 L157.6,92.2 L161.8,92.6 L166.0,93.0 L170.2,93.4 L174.4,93.8 L178.6,94.2 L182.8,94.5 L187.0,94.8 L191.2,95.1 L195.4,95.4 L199.6,95.6 L203.8,95.9 L208.0,96.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u1d62</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">positive recurrent:</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2211 \u03c0\u1d62 = 1, \u03bc\u1d62\u1d62 &lt; \u221e</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">null recurrent: \u03bc\u1d62\u1d62 = \u221e, \u03c0\u1d62 \u2261 0, no stationary law</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(e.g. the symmetric walk returns, but too slowly)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a long-run share needs finite expected return time</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Shares \u03c0\u1d62 in a positive recurrent chain add to one. For a null recurrent chain, such as the symmetric walk on the line, every \u03c0\u1d62 is 0 and no stationary law exists.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Positive Recurrence Criteria:</strong> An irreducible chain is positive recurrent if and only if $\\mu_{ii} = \\mathbb{E}[\\tau_i \\mid X_0 = i] \\lt  \\infty$ for some (and hence all) states $i$. In this case and only this case, a valid normalized probability distribution $\\pi$ exists satisfying $\\sum \\pi_i = 1$.",
      "<strong>Null Recurrence & Mass Dispersion:</strong> A chain is null recurrent if return probability is 1 ($f_{ii} = 1$), but expected return time is infinite ($\\mu_{ii} = \\infty$). Stationary equations $\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$ have non-trivial non-negative solutions, but their sum is infinite, yielding zero probability $\\pi_i = 1/\\infty = 0$ upon normalization.",
      "<strong>Reflected Random Walk Benchmark:</strong> On $\\mathbb{Z}_+$ with $P_{i, i+1} = p$ and $P_{i, i-1} = 1-p$: positive recurrent if $p \\lt  1/2$ (geometric stationary distribution); null recurrent if $p = 1/2$ (symmetric random walk wanders to infinity); transient if $p > 1/2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mu_{ii} \\lt  \\infty \\iff \\text{Pos. Recurrent } (\\sum \\pi_i = 1); \\quad \\mu_{ii} = \\infty \\iff \\text{Null Recurrent } (\\pi_i \\equiv 0)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Sure to come back, but too slowly.</strong> A walker on an endless street returns to the start for sure, but the average wait is infinite. So there is no steady share of days at the start, even though it keeps being visited.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming recurrence implies existence of a stationary distribution! On infinite state spaces, symmetric random walks are recurrent (f_00 = 1) but possess NO stationary probability distribution because \u03bc_00 = \u221e.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Positive versus null recurrence.</b> A recurrent state $i$ is positive recurrent if $\\mu_{ii}=\\mathbb E[\\tau_i\\mid X_0=i]\\lt \\infty$ and null recurrent if $\\mu_{ii}=\\infty$. An irreducible chain has a stationary distribution iff it is positive recurrent; for null recurrent or transient chains $\\pi_i\\equiv0$ (e.g. the symmetric random walk) (Ross 4.4; Grimmett 6.4).",
    "hint": "You return for sure, but can the waiting time be so long that no long-run share exists?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mu_{ii}\\lt \\infty$ = positive recurrent.</strong> The expected time to return is finite, so a positive fraction of days is spent at $i$.",
      "<strong>$\\mu_{ii}=\\infty$ = null recurrent.</strong> You return for sure but the expected wait is infinite, so the long-run share is zero.",
      "<strong>Stationary $\\pi$ exists iff positive recurrent.</strong> In the null recurrent case the limits $\\pi_i$ are all 0 and cannot add to one."
    ],
