    "title": "Cut Equations & Detailed Balance Equations",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32004\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">O</text><circle cx=\"180.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">L</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"14\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"72.0\" y1=\"44.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"44.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32004)\"/><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"72.0\" y2=\"56.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32004)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2092 P\u2092\u2097  \u2192</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2190  \u03c0\u2097 P\u2097\u2092</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">cut A | A\u1d9c</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">flow across any cut balances: \u2211 \u03c0\u1d62P\u1d62\u2c7c (i\u2208A, j\u2208A\u1d9c) = \u2211 \u03c0\u2c7cP\u2c7c\u1d62</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">detailed balance \u03c0\u1d62P\u1d62\u2c7c = \u03c0\u2c7cP\u2c7c\u1d62 \u21d2 \u03c0\u1d40P = \u03c0\u1d40</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(2/3)(0.2) = (1/3)(0.4) = 2/15</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The cut between on time and late. In steady state the rate on time \u2192 late, \u03c0\u2092P\u2092\u2097, equals the rate late \u2192 on time, \u03c0\u2097P\u2097\u2092 (both 2/15).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Global Cut Conservation Law:</strong> For any partition of state space $S = A \\cup A^c$, the net steady-state probability flux leaving $A$ must equal the flux entering $A$: $\\sum_{i \\in A} \\sum_{j \\in A^c} \\pi_i P_{ij} = \\sum_{j \\in A^c} \\sum_{i \\in A} \\pi_j P_{ji}$. This generalizes component balance.",
      "<strong>Detailed Balance Condition:</strong> A distribution $\\pi$ satisfies detailed balance if $\\pi_i P_{ij} = \\pi_j P_{ji}$ for all pairs $i, j \\in S$. Any non-negative normalized solution to detailed balance automatically satisfies full balance $\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$, making the Markov chain time-reversible.",
      "<strong>Birth-Death Process Simplification:</strong> In birth-death chains (transitions only to adjacent neighbors $i \\pm 1$), cut equations between $\\{0, \\dots, i\\}$ and $\\{i+1, \\dots\\}$ reduce directly to pairwise detailed balance $\\pi_i P_{i, i+1} = \\pi_{i+1} P_{i+1, i}$, bypassing full matrix inversion."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\sum_{i \\in A, j \\in A^c} \\pi_i P_{ij} = \\sum_{j \\in A^c, i \\in A} \\pi_j P_{ji}; \\quad \\text{Detailed Balance: } \\pi_i P_{ij} = \\pi_j P_{ji} \\implies \\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Balance the traffic.</strong> Of all days, $\\frac23$ are on time and $\\frac15$ of those are followed by a late day, $\\frac13$ are late and $\\frac25$ of those are followed by an on-time day: both flows are $\\frac2{15}$.",
    "examTrap": "Thinking all Markov chains satisfy detailed balance! Detailed balance only holds for *reversible* chains (such as trees or birth-death chains). Unidirectional cyclic chains (1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 1) satisfy global balance but violate detailed balance!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Cut equations and detailed balance.</b> If $\\pi$ is stationary then for every $A\\subset S$, $\\sum_{i\\in A,\\,j\\in A^c}\\pi_iP_{ij}=\\sum_{j\\in A^c,\\,i\\in A}\\pi_jP_{ji}$. If $\\pi_iP_{ij}=\\pi_jP_{ji}$ for all $i,j$ (detailed balance), then $\\pi^{\\top}P=\\pi^{\\top}$ and the chain is reversible (Ross 4.8; Grimmett 6.5).",
    "hint": "How can you find the steady split by balancing the traffic between two groups of mornings?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum_{i\\in A,j\\in A^c}\\pi_iP_{ij}$ = flow out of $A$.</strong> The long-run rate of moves from a set $A$ to its complement.",
      "<strong>= flow back into $A$.</strong> In a steady state what leaves a set must return at the same rate.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_iP_{ij}=\\pi_jP_{ji}$ = detailed balance.</strong> If every pair of states balances individually, summing over $i$ gives $\\pi_j=\\sum_i\\pi_iP_{ij}$."
    ],
