    "title": "Periodic DTMCs & Ces\u00e0ro Time-Average Convergence",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32005\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"70.0\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">O</text><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">L</text><line x1=\"82.0\" y1=\"54.0\" x2=\"148.0\" y2=\"54.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32005)\"/><line x1=\"148.0\" y1=\"66.0\" x2=\"82.0\" y2=\"66.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32005)\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">flip every day: period 2</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u207f never settles:</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">O, L, O, L, \u2026</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(1/N) \u2211\u2099 P\u1d62\u2c7c\u207d\u207f\u207e \u2192 \u03c0\u2c7c even for a periodic chain</text><text x=\"117.7\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the average over days converges, though the daily chance does not</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0 = (\u00bd, \u00bd)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A chain that flips O, L, O, L, \u2026 has period 2: P\u207f oscillates for ever, but the average over days converges to \u03c0 = (\u00bd, \u00bd).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Failure of Pointwise Limits:</strong> For an irreducible positive-recurrent chain with period $d > 1$, the state space partitions into cyclic classes $C_0, \\dots, C_{d-1}$. The sequence of transition probabilities $P_{ij}^{(n)}$ oscillates periodically and fails to converge to any single constant.",
      "<strong>Ces\u00e0ro Limit Universality:</strong> Even when periodicity destroys the ordinary limit, the Ces\u00e0ro time-average limit always exists and equals the unique stationary distribution: $\\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{n=1}^N P_{ij}^{(n)} = \\pi_j$ for all states $i, j$.",
      "<strong>Stationary Vector Invariance:</strong> The stationary vector $\\pi$ satisfying $\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$ remains completely valid and unique for periodic positive recurrent chains; periodicity affects pathwise synchronization, not steady-state invariant measures."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{n=1}^N P_{ij}^{(n)} = \\pi_j \\quad (\\text{holds for both periodic and aperiodic positive recurrent chains})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Alternating days still have a share.</strong> If good and bad days strictly alternate, the chance of a good day tomorrow is 0 or 1, never settling. But the fraction of good days among many is steady at one half.",
    "examTrap": "Claiming a periodic chain has no stationary distribution! Periodicity only prevents pointwise convergence lim_{n \u2192 \u221e} P_ij^(n); the stationary distribution \u03c0 still exists and satisfies \u03c0^T P = \u03c0^T uniquely!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Periodic chains and Ces\u00e0ro limits.</b> For an irreducible positive recurrent chain, periodic or not, $\\lim_{N\\to\\infty}\\frac1N\\sum_{n=1}^NP^{(n)}_{ij}=\\pi_j$. If the chain has period $d\\gt 1$, $P^{(n)}_{ij}$ itself does not converge (Ross 4.4; Grimmett 6.4).",
    "hint": "If the chain flips back and forth with a fixed rhythm, in what sense does it still settle?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$P^{(n)}_{ij}$ may oscillate.</strong> A strictly alternating chain has $P^{(n)}_{ii}=1,0,1,0,\\ldots$, with no limit.",
      "<strong>$\\frac1N\\sum_{n=1}^NP^{(n)}_{ij}$ = the time average of the chances.</strong> Averaging over the days flattens the oscillation.",
      "<strong>$\\to\\pi_j$ = the long-run share still exists.</strong> The Ces\u00e0ro limit is $\\pi_j$ for every irreducible positive recurrent chain."
    ],
