    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32101\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"36.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B</text><circle cx=\"76.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><circle cx=\"116.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><circle cx=\"156.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3</text><circle cx=\"196.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><line x1=\"48.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"64.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"48.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"88.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"128.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"144.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"144.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"128.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"184.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><line x1=\"184.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32101)\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">interior stops</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">give up</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">campus</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a\u1d62 = \u2211\u2c7c P\u1d62\u2c7c a\u2c7c for i interior; a\u1d62 = 1 on A, 0 on B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">condition on the first step, then repeat</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a\u1d62 = \u2119(reach A before B | start at i)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A line of stops between giving up (B) and campus (A). The chance a\u1d62 of reaching A first satisfies a\u1d62 = \u2211\u2c7c P\u1d62\u2c7c a\u2c7c with a\u1d62 = 1 on A and 0 on B.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Total Probability Decomposition:</strong> To find absorption probability $a_i = P(\\tau_A \\lt  \\tau_B \\mid X_0 = i)$, condition on the very first jump $X_1 = j$. By the Markov property, the process restarts from state $j$, yielding linear balance $a_i = \\sum_{j \\in S} P_{ij} a_j$.",
      "<strong>Boundary Pinning Conditions:</strong> The linear system requires explicit boundary values: $a_i = 1$ for all target states $i \\in A$, and $a_i = 0$ for all competing absorbing states $i \\in B$. For transient states $i \\notin A \\cup B$, $a_i$ lies strictly in $(0, 1)$.",
      "<strong>Uniqueness via Maximum Principle:</strong> In finite state spaces where absorption occurs with probability 1 from all transient states, the linear system $(I - Q) a = R_A$ has a unique solution because all eigenvalues of sub-stochastic matrix $Q$ satisfy $|\\lambda| \\lt  1$."
    ],
    "math": "$$a_i = \\sum_{j \\in S} P_{ij} a_j \\quad (i \\notin A \\cup B), \\quad a_i = 1 \\ (i \\in A), \\quad a_i = 0 \\ (i \\in B)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Look one stop ahead.</strong> The chance of reaching campus from stop 2 is the average of the chances from the stops you may move to. Solving these linear equations gives every stop's chance at once.",
    "examTrap": "Forgetting to check boundary conditions! If boundary states a_i = 1 are omitted, the trivial all-zero vector a_i \u2261 0 solves the unconstrained system a = P a. Always specify boundary conditions on absorbing sets!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>First-step analysis for absorption.</b> Let $A,B\\subset S$ be disjoint absorbing sets and $a_i=\\mathbb P_i(\\text{hit }A\\text{ before }B)$. Then $a_i=\\sum_{j\\in S}P_{ij}a_j$ for $i\\notin A\\cup B$, with $a_i=1$ for $i\\in A$ and $a_i=0$ for $i\\in B$. The minimal non-negative solution is $a_i$ (Ross 4.5; Grimmett 6.3).",
    "hint": "How do you find the chance of reaching campus before giving up by looking one stop ahead?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$a_i=\\mathbb P_i(\\text{hit }A\\text{ before }B)$ = the target chance.</strong> Start at stop $i$; $a_i$ is the chance you reach campus before turning back.",
      "<strong>$a_i=\\sum_jP_{ij}a_j$ = condition on the first step.</strong> After one move you are at $j$ and the problem starts afresh from there.",
      "<strong>$a_i=1$ on $A$, $a_i=0$ on $B$ = boundary values.</strong> Already at campus, success is certain; already home, it is impossible."
    ],
