    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32102\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"36.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B</text><circle cx=\"76.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><circle cx=\"116.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><circle cx=\"156.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3</text><circle cx=\"196.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A</text><line x1=\"48.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"64.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"48.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"88.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"128.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"144.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"144.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"128.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"184.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><line x1=\"184.0\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32102)\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">each step costs one minute</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u1d62 = 0 on A</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u1d62 = 1 + \u2211\u2c7c\u2209A P\u1d62\u2c7c \u03bc\u2c7c elsewhere</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21d4 (I \u2212 Q) \u03bc = 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u1d62 = expected steps to hit A</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The same line of stops with a cost of 1 for each step. The expected time to reach campus satisfies \u03bc\u1d62 = 1 + \u2211\u2c7c P\u1d62\u2c7c \u03bc\u2c7c with \u03bc = 0 at campus.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>First-Step Time Accumulation:</strong> The expected hitting time to target set $A$, $\\mu_i = \\mathbb{E}[\\tau_A \\mid X_0 = i]$, satisfies $\\mu_i = 1 + \\sum_{j \\in S} P_{ij} \\mu_j$ for $i \\notin A$. The constant '$+1$' accounts for elapsed time of the initial transition step.",
      "<strong>Target Boundary Condition:</strong> By definition, if the chain begins already inside target set $A$, zero additional steps are required: $\\mu_i = 0$ for all $i \\in A$. This provides essential non-homogeneous anchoring for the linear equation system.",
      "<strong>Matrix Formulation:</strong> In vector form over transient states $T$, the system is $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\mathbf{1} + Q \\boldsymbol{\\mu}$, which yields $(I - Q) \\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\mathbf{1} \\implies \\boldsymbol{\\mu} = (I - Q)^{-1} \\mathbf{1}$, identifying mean hitting time as the row sum of the fundamental matrix."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mu_i = \\begin{cases} 0 & i \\in A \\\\ 1 + \\sum_{j \\notin A} P_{ij} \\mu_j & i \\notin A \\end{cases} \\iff (I - Q) \\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\mathbf{1}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Counting minutes to campus.</strong> The expected time from a stop is one minute plus the average of the expected times from where you land. Solving the system gives the expected trip time from every stop.",
    "examTrap": "Omitting the +1 in hitting time calculations! Without +1, the equation becomes \u03bc = Q\u03bc, which gives the useless trivial solution \u03bc = 0. In contrast, absorption probabilities do NOT have +1.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Mean hitting time.</b> Let $\\mu_i=\\mathbb E_i[\\tau_A]$ be the expected number of steps to hit $A$. It is the minimal non-negative solution of $\\mu_i=0$ for $i\\in A$ and $\\mu_i=1+\\sum_{j\\notin A}P_{ij}\\mu_j$ for $i\\notin A$; equivalently $(I-Q)\\boldsymbol\\mu=\\mathbf 1$, with $Q$ the transitions among states outside $A$ (Ross 4.5; Grimmett 6.3).",
    "hint": "How many minutes does the trip take on average, counted one step at a time?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mu_i=\\mathbb E_i[\\tau_A]$ = the average journey time.</strong> The expected number of steps from stop $i$ until the first arrival in $A$.",
      "<strong>$\\mu_i=1+\\sum_jP_{ij}\\mu_j$ = pay one step, then continue.</strong> Every step costs one unit, then you are at $j$ with $\\mu_j$ left to go.",
      "<strong>$(I-Q)\\boldsymbol\\mu=\\mathbf 1$ = the same in matrix form.</strong> $Q$ is the part of $P$ that stays outside $A$; solving gives all $\\mu_i$."
    ],
