    "category": "MATRIX ABSORPTION CALCULUS",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Absorption Probabilities B = NR & Lifetime Vector",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32104\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"50.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">i</text><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">j</text><circle cx=\"190.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><line x1=\"62.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"108.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32104)\"/><line x1=\"132.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"178.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32104)\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">visits, then a jump into the trap</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">B = N R:  B\u1d62\u2096 = \u2119(absorbed in k | start at i)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">t = N 1:  t\u1d62 = \ud835\udd3c[time to absorption | start at i]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">visits to each interior stop \u00d7 chance of leaving from it,</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">summed over all stops</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "From stop i, N counts visits to each transient stop j and R gives the jump into an absorbing state k. So B = NR gives destinations and t = N1 the expected trip length.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Destination Matrix Product $B = NR$:</strong> The $(t \\times r)$ matrix $B$ provides exact absorption probabilities: $B_{ik} = P(\\text{absorbed in state } k \\mid X_0 = i) = (NR)_{ik}$. Every row of $B$ sums to 1 if absorption occurs with probability 1 from all transient states.",
      "<strong>Expected Time to Absorption Vector:</strong> The total duration spent wandering through all transient states before absorption is obtained by summing expected visits across all transient states: $t_i = \\sum_{j \\in T} N_{ij} = (N \\mathbf{1})_i$.",
      "<strong>Direct Computational Advantage:</strong> Inverting a single $(t \\times t)$ matrix $(I - Q)$ simultaneously evaluates absorption probabilities into all sinks and expected lifetimes from all starting states, eliminating piecemeal linear equations."
    ],
    "math": "$$B = N R \\implies B_{ik} = P(\\text{Absorbed into } k \\mid X_0 = i); \\quad \\mathbf{t} = N \\mathbf{1} \\implies t_i = \\mathbb{E}[\\tau_{\\text{abs}} \\mid X_0 = i]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Destination and duration.</strong> From the visit counter you read both the chance of finishing at campus rather than at home, and the expected length of the whole trip.",
    "examTrap": "Multiplying RN instead of NR! The dimensions must align: N is (t \u00d7 t) and R is (t \u00d7 r), so NR produces a (t \u00d7 r) matrix mapping transient starting states to absorbing destinations. RN is undefined!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Absorption probabilities and lifetime.</b> With $N=(I-Q)^{-1}$, the matrix $B=NR$ has entries $B_{ik}=\\mathbb P_i(\\text{absorbed in state }k)$, and the vector $\\mathbf t=N\\mathbf 1$ has $t_i=\\mathbb E_i[\\tau_{\\text{abs}}]$, the expected time to absorption (Grimmett 6.3; Kemeny\u2013Snell).",
    "hint": "Where do you end up, and how long does it take, from the fundamental matrix alone?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$B=NR$ = visits times exit chances.</strong> Visit each transient stop $j$ $N_{ij}$ times on average, and each visit exits to $k$ with chance $R_{jk}$.",
      "<strong>$B_{ik}=\\mathbb P_i(\\text{absorbed in }k)$ = the destination law.</strong> Each row of $B$ adds to one.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbf t=N\\mathbf 1$ = total visits = total time.</strong> Every step is a visit to some transient state, so summing a row of $N$ counts the steps."
    ],
