    "title": "Pattern Waiting Times & The Self-Overlap Paradox",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32106\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"40.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2205</text><circle cx=\"100.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">H</text><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"12.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">HT</text><line x1=\"52.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32106)\"/><line x1=\"112.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"148.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32106)\"/><circle cx=\"40.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2205</text><circle cx=\"100.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">H</text><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"12.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">HH</text><line x1=\"52.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32106)\"/><line x1=\"112.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"148.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32106)\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[T] = 4</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[T] = 6</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[TW] = \u2211\u2c7c c\u2c7c 2\u02b2, summed over self-overlaps</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(Conway: the overlapping pattern waits longer)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Two absorbing chains of partial matches: \u2205 \u2192 H \u2192 HT and \u2205 \u2192 H \u2192 HH. Self-overlap makes HH slower: \ud835\udd3c[T] = 6 compared with 4.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Prefix State Automata:</strong> Model the occurrence of sequence pattern $W$ as hitting time of an absorbing Markov chain whose states represent the longest matched prefix of $W$. Transitions follow incoming coin tosses.",
      "<strong>The $HT$ vs $HH$ Paradox:</strong> In fair coin tosses, $\\mathbb{E}[T_{HT}] = 4$ whereas $\\mathbb{E}[T_{HH}] = 6$. For $HT$: if an $H$ is followed by $H$, the match prefix remains length 1 ($H$), maintaining forward readiness. For $HH$: if $H$ is followed by $T$, the prefix collapses completely to $\\emptyset$.",
      "<strong>Conway\u2019s Pattern Leading Number Rule:</strong> The expected waiting time for any binary pattern $W$ of length $k$ is $\\mathbb{E}[T_W] = \\sum_{j=1}^k c_j 2^j$, where $c_j = 1$ if the prefix of length $j$ matches the suffix of length $j$ (self-overlap), and 0 otherwise."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}[T_{HT}] = 4 \\quad \\text{vs} \\quad \\mathbb{E}[T_{HH}] = 6; \\quad \\mathbb{E}[T_W] = \\sum_{j=1}^k c_j 2^j \\quad (\\text{Conway's Theorem})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Waiting for a pattern of days.</strong> Waiting for two late days in a row takes longer, on average, than waiting for late then on time, because the second \u2018late\u2019 in a failed attempt can't be reused as the start of a new one.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming equally likely sequences have equal expected waiting times! At any two consecutive flips, P(HT) = P(HH) = 1/4, but waiting times differ fundamentally due to renewal regeneration: after seeing HH, another H immediately completes the next HH in 1 flip, clustering occurrences together!",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Pattern waiting times.</b> For fair coin tosses, $\\mathbb E[T_{HT}]=4$ but $\\mathbb E[T_{HH}]=6$. In general, for a pattern $W$ of length $k$, $\\mathbb E[T_W]=\\sum_{j=1}^kc_j2^j$ where $c_j=1$ if the first $j$ letters of $W$ equal its last $j$ letters, and $0$ otherwise (Conway; Grimmett 6.3).",
    "hint": "Why does waiting for two heads in a row take longer than waiting for heads then tails?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[T_{HT}]=4$ = no overlap.</strong> After an H you are one toss from success; a wrong toss just restarts with a partial match.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[T_{HH}]=6$ = self-overlap.</strong> After H then T you lose all progress; failing at HH costs more than failing at HT.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_jc_j2^j$ = Conway's formula.</strong> Sum $2^j$ over each prefix $j$ equal to the same-length suffix; here $HH$ gives $2+4=6$, and $HT$ gives only $4$."
    ],
