    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Gibbs Sampling & Full Conditional Updates",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32206\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32206)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32206)\"/><path d=\"M60.0,100.0 L60.0,72.0 L112.0,72.0 L112.0,50.0 L164.0,50.0 L164.0,34.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"34\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><text x=\"224\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">one coordinate at a time</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">draw X\u1d62 ~ p(X\u1d62 | X\u208b\u1d62): always accepted, \u03b1 \u2261 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(the path moves along the axes)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A Gibbs path moves along the axes: update x\u2081 given x\u2082, then x\u2082 given x\u2081. Each update is a draw from a full conditional and is always accepted (\u03b1 \u2261 1).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Coordinate-Wise Iteration:</strong> To sample from joint distribution $p(x_1, \\dots, x_d)$, Gibbs sampling updates each variable sequentially by sampling from its full conditional distribution: $X_i^{(t+1)} \\sim p(X_i \\mid X_1^{(t+1)}, \\dots, X_{i-1}^{(t+1)}, X_{i+1}^{(t)}, \\dots, X_d^{(t)})$.",
      "<strong>Special Case of Metropolis-Hastings:</strong> Gibbs sampling is mathematically a Metropolis-Hastings algorithm where proposal is the exact conditional $q(y \\mid x) = p(y_i \\mid x_{-i})$. Substituting this proposal into the M-H ratio yields an acceptance probability of identically 1: $\\alpha(x, y) = \\min(1, 1) = 1$.",
      "<strong>AR(1) Dynamics in Gaussian Models:</strong> When applying Gibbs sampling to standard bivariate Gaussian $(X, Y)$ with correlation $\rho$, each variable is updated as $X_{t+1} = \\rho^2 X_t + \\sqrt{1 - \\rho^4} Z_t$, establishing an exact AR(1) process with convergence speed determined by $\\rho^2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$X_i^{(t+1)} \\sim p(X_i \\mid X_{-i}^{(t)}) \\implies \\alpha(x, y) = \\min\\left(1, \\frac{p(y) p(x_i \\mid x_{-i})}{p(x) p(y_i \\mid x_{-i})}\\right) \\equiv 1$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Fix one, redraw the other.</strong> Given the wait time, redraw the ride time from its conditional law; then given the ride time, redraw the wait. Alternating the two samples the pair jointly, with nothing thrown away.",
    "examTrap": "Applying Gibbs sampling when full conditionals are not analytically standard! Gibbs sampling requires easy sampling from 1D full conditionals p(X_i | X_{-i}). If conditionals are intractable, Metropolis-within-Gibbs must be used instead.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Gibbs sampling.</b> To sample $p(x_1,\\ldots,x_d)$, update one coordinate at a time from its full conditional: $X_i^{(t+1)}\\sim p(X_i\\mid X_{-i}^{(t)})$. This is Metropolis\u2013Hastings with proposal $q(y\\mid x)=p(y_i\\mid x_{-i})$, for which the acceptance probability is $\\alpha(x,y)\\equiv1$, so every proposal is accepted (Robert & Casella 10; Grimmett 6.14).",
    "hint": "Can you sample a joint law by redrawing one variable at a time, never rejecting?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$X_i\\sim p(X_i\\mid X_{-i})$ = redraw one coordinate.</strong> Hold all the others fixed and resample from the exact conditional law.",
      "<strong>$\\alpha(x,y)=\\min\\bigl(1,\\frac{p(y)p(x_i\\mid x_{-i})}{p(x)p(y_i\\mid x_{-i})}\\bigr)$ = the MH ratio.</strong> Since $y_{-i}=x_{-i}$ and $p(y)=p(y_i\\mid x_{-i})p(x_{-i})$, the ratio equals 1.",
      "<strong>$\\alpha\\equiv1$ = never rejected.</strong> Each update is a valid move of a chain with stationary law $p$."
    ],
