    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "The Order Statistics Property & Uniform Conditioning",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32403\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"44\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">given n buses in [0, t]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">arrival times = n sorted uniform draws on (0, t)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">joint density n!/t\u207f on 0 &lt; s\u2081 &lt; \u2026 &lt; s\u2099 &lt; t</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[S\u2096 | N(t) = n] = k t / (n + 1)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the n buses split the hour into n + 1 equal-ish gaps</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Given N(t) = n, the n arrivals are like n uniform points on (0, t), sorted. The k-th arrival is on average k/(n + 1) of the way through.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Uniform Order Statistics Theorem:</strong> Given that exactly $n$ arrivals occurred in $[0, t]$, the unordered arrival times $U_1, \\dots, U_n$ are mutually independent and identically distributed as $\\text{Uniform}[0, t]$. Consequently, $(S_1, \\dots, S_n)$ are the order statistics $U_{(1)} \\le \\dots \\le U_{(n)}$.",
      "<strong>Constant Joint Conditional Density:</strong> The joint conditional density is constant over the simplex $0 \\lt  s_1 \\lt  s_2 \\lt  \\dots \\lt  s_n \\lt  t$: $f_{S_1, \\dots, S_n \\mid N(t)=n}(s_1, \\dots, s_n) = \\frac{n!}{t^n}$, where $n!$ accounts for the permutations of unordered uniforms.",
      "<strong>Marginal Conditional Expectations:</strong> Using properties of uniform order statistics, the conditional expected arrival time of the $k$-th customer is evenly spaced: $\\mathbb{E}[S_k \\mid N(t) = n] = \\frac{k}{n+1} t$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{S_1, \\dots, S_n \\mid N(t) = n}(s_1, \\dots, s_n) = \\frac{n!}{t^n} \\quad (0 \\lt  s_1 \\lt  \\dots \\lt  s_n \\lt  t); \\quad \\mathbb{E}[S_k \\mid N(t) = n] = \\frac{k}{n+1}t$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Where did the three buses fall?</strong> If exactly 3 buses came in an hour, they are like 3 darts thrown uniformly at the hour; on average the middle one is at 30 minutes.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming arrivals are uniformly spaced deterministically! Conditioned on N(t) = n, arrival times are *random* order statistics with expected spacing t/(n+1), NOT equally spaced grid points k\u00b7t/n!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Order-statistics property.</b> Given $N(t)=n$, the arrival times $(S_1,\\ldots,S_n)$ have the law of the order statistics of $n$ i.i.d. $\\operatorname{Unif}(0,t)$ variables: the joint density is $\\frac{n!}{t^n}$ on $0\\lt s_1\\lt \\cdots\\lt s_n\\lt t$, and $\\mathbb E[S_k\\mid N(t)=n]=\\frac{k}{n+1}t$ (Ross 5.3; Grimmett 6.12).",
    "hint": "If you know exactly n buses came in the hour, where in the hour did they fall?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\frac{n!}{t^n}$ = uniform on the ordered region.</strong> Given the count, the times are exchangeable and spread evenly over $(0,t)$, then sorted.",
      "<strong>Order statistics of $n$ uniforms.</strong> The arrival times are just sorted independent uniform points.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[S_k\\mid N(t)=n]=\\frac k{n+1}t$ = evenly spaced on average.</strong> The $k$-th arrival is expected $k/(n+1)$ of the way through."
    ],
