    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32603\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32603)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32603)\"/><path d=\"M26.0,64.0 L32.5,68.0 L39.1,72.0 L45.6,68.0 L52.1,64.0 L58.7,60.0 L65.2,64.0 L71.7,60.0 L78.3,64.0 L84.8,60.0 L91.3,64.0 L97.9,60.0 L104.4,64.0 L110.9,68.0 L117.5,64.0 L124.0,68.0 L130.5,72.0 L137.1,68.0 L143.6,72.0 L150.1,76.0 L156.7,72.0 L163.2,76.0 L169.7,80.0 L176.3,84.0 L182.8,80.0 L189.3,76.0 L195.9,80.0 L202.4,84.0 L208.9,80.0 L215.5,76.0 L222.0,72.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"117.46666666666667\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"117.46666666666667\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><circle cx=\"117.46666666666667\" cy=\"64\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"117.46666666666667\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c4</text><path d=\"M117.5,64.0 L222.0,64.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">stop when the delay first hits a rule</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">{\u03c4 \u2264 n} \u2208 \u2131\u2099: the decision uses only what is known by day n</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">M\u2099\u2227\u03c4 is a martingale and \ud835\udd3c[M\u2099\u2227\u03c4] = \ud835\udd3c[M\u2080]</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A tally, stopped at the first time \u03c4 a rule is met. The stopped tally M\u2099\u2227\u03c4 follows the path until \u03c4 and then stays put; it is still a martingale.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Formal Stopping Time Axiom:</strong> A random variable $\\tau \\in \\{0, 1, 2, \\dots\\} \\cup \\{\\infty\\}$ is a stopping time with respect to filtration $\\mathbb{F}$ if the event of stopping by time $n$ is completely determined by history up to time $n$: $\\{\\tau \\le n\\} \\in \\mathcal{F}_n$ for all $n \\ge 0$.",
      "<strong>No Crystal Ball Principle:</strong> A valid stopping rule cannot look into the future. For example, 'stop at the first time wealth hits $\\$100$' is a stopping time; 'stop one step before the maximum wealth' is NOT a stopping time.",
      "<strong>Stability Under Stopping:</strong> If $M_n$ is a martingale and $\\tau$ is a stopping time, the stopped process $M_n^\\tau = M_{n \\wedge \\tau}$ is also a martingale. In particular, $\\mathbb{E}[M_{n \\wedge \\tau}] = \\mathbb{E}[M_0]$ for every finite truncation step $n$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\{\\tau \\le n\\} \\in \\mathcal{F}_n \\quad \\forall n \\ge 0 \\implies M_{n \\wedge \\tau} \\text{ is a Martingale}, \\quad \\mathbb{E}[M_{n \\wedge \\tau}] = \\mathbb{E}[M_0]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>No system beats a fair game.</strong> Leaving the first time the tally hits +10 minutes, or whenever you like based on the past, never changes your expected tally at a fixed day.",
    "examTrap": "Treating the last time a state is visited as a stopping time! The event 'last visit to 0' requires observing the entire infinite future to ensure the process never returns. It is NOT a stopping time!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Stopping times and the stopped martingale.</b> A random time $\\tau$ is a stopping time if $\\{\\tau\\le n\\}\\in\\mathcal F_n$ for all $n\\ge0$. If $(M_n)$ is a martingale then the stopped process $M_{n\\wedge\\tau}$ is a martingale, so $\\mathbb E[M_{n\\wedge\\tau}]=\\mathbb E[M_0]$ for each $n$ (Williams 10; Grimmett 12.4).",
    "hint": "If you decide when to stop using only what you know so far, does the game stay fair?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\{\\tau\\le n\\}\\in\\mathcal F_n$ = a decision from the past.</strong> Whether you have stopped by day $n$ is determined by the information up to day $n$; no peeking ahead.",
      "<strong>$M_{n\\wedge\\tau}$ = the tally frozen at $\\tau$.</strong> It follows $M$ until the stopping time and then stays put.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[M_{n\\wedge\\tau}]=\\mathbb E[M_0]$ = still fair.</strong> No rule that uses only the past can turn a fair game into a favourable one, at any fixed horizon $n$."
    ],
