    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32605\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32605)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32605)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n</text><path d=\"M26.0,66.0 L30.6,61.0 L35.1,56.0 L39.7,51.0 L44.2,56.0 L48.8,51.0 L53.3,56.0 L57.9,61.0 L62.4,56.0 L67.0,61.0 L71.6,66.0 L76.1,61.0 L80.7,56.0 L85.2,61.0 L89.8,56.0 L94.3,61.0 L98.9,56.0 L103.4,51.0 L108.0,46.0 L112.6,51.0 L117.1,56.0 L121.7,61.0 L126.2,66.0 L130.8,61.0 L135.3,66.0 L139.9,61.0 L144.4,56.0 L149.0,61.0 L153.6,66.0 L158.1,61.0 L162.7,56.0 L167.2,51.0 L171.8,46.0 L176.3,41.0 L180.9,46.0 L185.4,41.0 L190.0,46.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"34\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"34\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">+b</text><text x=\"224\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2212a</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">S\u2099</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[S_\u03c4] = 0 \u21d2 \u2119(hit +b first) = a/(a + b)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[S_\u03c4\u00b2 \u2212 \u03c4] = 0 \u21d2 \ud835\udd3c[\u03c4] = ab</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(fair walk between \u2212a and +b)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A fair walk exits the corridor (\u2212a, b) at \u03c4. The martingale S\u2099 gives \u2119(hit +b) = a/(a+b); the martingale S\u2099\u00b2 \u2212 n gives \ud835\udd3c[\u03c4] = ab.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Gambler\u2019s Ruin Exit Probability:</strong> For a symmetric random walk starting at 0 with absorption at $+a$ or $-b$, $M_n = S_n$ is a bounded martingale up to stopping time $\\tau$. By OST: $\\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau] = p_a(a) + (1 - p_a)(-b) = S_0 = 0 \\implies p_a = \\frac{b}{a+b}$.",
      "<strong>Expected Game Duration via Variance Martingale:</strong> Applying OST to the variance martingale $M_n = S_n^2 - n$ with stopped value $S_\\tau^2$: $\\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau^2 - \\tau] = 0 \\implies \\mathbb{E}[\\tau] = \\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau^2] = p_a(a^2) + (1-p_a)(-b)^2 = \\frac{b}{a+b}a^2 + \\frac{a}{a+b}b^2 = ab$.",
      "<strong>Wald\u2019s First & Second Identities:</strong> When $\\tau$ is a stopping time with $\\mathbb{E}[\\tau] \\lt  \\infty$, applying OST to compensated martingales immediately rederives Wald's equations: $\\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau] = \\mathbb{E}[\\tau]\\mathbb{E}[X]$ and $\\mathbb{E}[(S_\\tau - \\tau\\mu)^2] = \\sigma^2 \\mathbb{E}[\\tau]$ without renewal convolutions."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau] = 0 \\implies p_a = \\frac{b}{a+b}; \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[S_\\tau^2 - \\tau] = 0 \\implies \\mathbb{E}[\\tau] = ab \\quad (\\text{Fair Random Walk})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The corridor.</strong> A fair walker between a door at $-a$ and a door at $+b$ reaches the far door with chance $a/(a+b)$, and takes $ab$ steps on average. Two fair-game tallies answer both questions.",
    "examTrap": "Applying E[\u03c4] = ab to biased walks! The identity E[S_\u03c4\u00b2 - \u03c4] = 0 holds ONLY for zero-mean symmetric walks (p = 1/2). For biased walks (p \u2260 1/2), you must use the exponential Wald martingale exp(\u03b8 S_n) / (M(\u03b8))^n instead!",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Gambler's ruin by OST.</b> For a fair simple random walk $S_n$ started at $0$ and $\\tau$ the first exit time from $(-a,b)$: $\\mathbb E[S_\\tau]=0$ gives $\\mathbb P(\\text{hit }b\\text{ first})=\\frac a{a+b}$, and $\\mathbb E[S_\\tau^2-\\tau]=0$ gives $\\mathbb E[\\tau]=ab$ (Wald's identities) (Ross 6.3; Williams 10.12).",
    "hint": "How do the two fair-game tallies give the chance of success and the expected duration at once?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[S_\\tau]=0$ = the walk is a martingale.</strong> The stopped value is $b$ with chance $p$ and $-a$ with chance $1-p$, so $pb-(1-p)a=0$.",
      "<strong>$p=\\frac a{a+b}$ = the chance of reaching $+b$ first.</strong> Solving $pb=(1-p)a$ gives the fractional position of the start between the two ends.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[S_\\tau^2-\\tau]=0\\Rightarrow\\mathbb E[\\tau]=ab$ = expected duration.</strong> $\\mathbb E[S_\\tau^2]=pb^2+(1-p)a^2=ab$."
    ],
