    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Stationary Distribution \u03c0 & Global vs Detailed Balance",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32704\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><circle cx=\"180.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><line x1=\"72.0\" y1=\"44.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"44.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32704)\"/><line x1=\"168.0\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"72.0\" y2=\"56.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32704)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2081 q\u2081\u2082</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2082 q\u2082\u2081</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">flow out of a state = flow in</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">global: \u03c0\u1d40Q = 0\u1d40, \u2211 \u03c0\u1d62 = 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">detailed: \u03c0\u1d62 q\u1d62\u2c7c = \u03c0\u2c7c q\u2c7c\u1d62 \u21d2 \u03c0\u1d40Q = 0\u1d40</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">balance of rates (not chances): no uniformisation needed</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Flow between two states: rate out of 1 is \u03c0\u2081q\u2081\u2082 and rate into 1 is \u03c0\u2082q\u2082\u2081. At the stationary law they are equal, which is detailed balance.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Global Balance Invariant:</strong> A probability vector $\\pi$ is stationary for a CTMC if $\\pi^\\top P(t) = \\pi^\\top$ for all $t \\ge 0$. Differentiating at $t=0$ yields $\\pi^\\top Q = \\mathbf{0}^\\top$ subject to $\\sum_i \\pi_i = 1$ and $\\pi_i > 0$.",
      "<strong>Component-wise Inflow = Outflow:</strong> Expanding $\\pi^\\top Q = \\mathbf{0}^\\top$ yields $\\sum_{i \\ne j} \\pi_i q_{ij} = \\pi_j q_j = \\pi_j \\sum_{k \\ne j} q_{jk}$ for every state $j$. Total rate of probability flow entering state $j$ equals total rate leaving state $j$.",
      "<strong>Continuous Detailed Balance:</strong> If a distribution satisfies pairwise detailed balance $\\pi_i q_{ij} = \\pi_j q_{ji}$ for all $i \\ne j$, then summing over $i$ immediately satisfies global balance $\\pi^\\top Q = \\mathbf{0}^\\top$. Reversible CTMCs (like birth-death processes) satisfy detailed balance."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\pi^\\top Q = \\mathbf{0}^\\top, \\quad \\sum_{i \\in S} \\pi_i = 1; \\qquad \\text{Detailed Balance: } \\pi_i q_{ij} = \\pi_j q_{ji} \\implies \\pi^\\top Q = \\mathbf{0}^\\top$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Balance the rates.</strong> If the bus is on time for $\\frac23$ of the time and goes late at rate 2, while being late for $\\frac13$ of the time and recovering at rate 4, both flows are $\\frac43$ an hour: balanced.",
    "examTrap": "Using \u03c0^T Q = \u03c0^T instead of \u03c0^T Q = 0^T! In DTMC, \u03c0^T P = \u03c0^T. But in CTMC, generator Q has zero row sums, so the stationary equation is \u03c0^T Q = 0^T!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Stationary distribution of a CTMC.</b> A probability vector $\\pi$ is stationary if $\\pi^\\top Q=\\mathbf 0^\\top$ (global balance), $\\sum_i\\pi_i=1$, equivalently $\\pi^\\top P(t)=\\pi^\\top$ for all $t$. If $\\pi_iq_{ij}=\\pi_jq_{ji}$ for all $i,j$ (detailed balance), then $\\pi^\\top Q=\\mathbf 0^\\top$ (Ross 6.5; Grimmett 6.9).",
    "hint": "Which split of time between states is unchanged by the switching?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\pi^\\top Q=\\mathbf 0^\\top$ = global balance.</strong> For each state, the rate of flow in, $\\sum_i\\pi_iq_{ij}$, equals the rate of flow out, $\\pi_jq_j$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_i\\pi_i=1$ = a split of time.</strong> $\\pi_i$ is the long-run fraction of time in state $i$.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_iq_{ij}=\\pi_jq_{ji}$ = detailed balance.</strong> If every pair of states balances individually, summing over $i$ gives global balance."
    ],
